@init
ext_noinit = 1.0;
ext_tail_size = -1;

// Borderless embed in the TCP / MCP (REAPER 7.45+). Swing was the only EON
// JSFX not asking for this, which is why it alone carried a title strip in the
// mixer — EON_Drum_Strip, EON_FX_Return_View and EON_StepSeq all set it.
// ⚠️ MUST be set in @init: writing it later has no effect. jsfx-lint flags this
//    as wrong_context — its model predates 7.45, and the other three EON JSFX
//    raise the identical warning. Accepted, not a defect.
// ⛔ Copy ONLY this line from them. The retina-scaling flag that sits next to it
//    in those files stays off in Swing (named nowhere here on purpose, so the
//    standing "is it absent?" grep keeps returning clean).
// 0x400 = suppress REAPER's hover tooltip over the MCP embed (7.79+; older ignores).
// House rule 1 (wiki 4.5): 0x100 = no REAPER frame and no grey name bar over the
// embed, 0x400 = no MCP hover tooltip. The bar is now a per-instance OPTION — the
// THEME menu's NAME BAR row, slider45, default 0 = borderless. REAPER's doc calls
// 0x100 an @init decision, so it is applied here from the restored slider; the
// per-pass re-apply in @gfx is what makes the row take effect without a reload
// (measured both ways on 7.79 and 7.80, .dev_tests/EON_Probe_EmbedBar_*).
gfx_ext_flags |= 0x400;
name_bar ? ( gfx_ext_flags = (gfx_ext_flags | 0x100) - 0x100; ) : ( gfx_ext_flags |= 0x100; );

// Generate unique instance ID (persists via slider4 + ext_noinit).
//
// Previous impl used `time_precise() * 100000` which had a 10µs
// collision window — two instances spawned in the same audio block on
// project load could end up with identical IDs (e.g. opening an old
// project authored before instance_id was added, where both saved
// slider4=0). All multi-instance routing breaks if IDs collide.
//
// New impl: gmem[KIT_GMEM_INSTANCE_NEXT] is a monotonic counter. Each
// instance reads the current value, writes value+1 back, takes that
// as its ID. JSFX @init runs sequentially on REAPER's main thread per
// audio block, so the read-write pair is naturally atomic within a
// single instance's init pass. Counter persists for the REAPER
// session (gmem outlives individual JSFX instances), and every instance
// raises it to its RESTORED id once REAPER has put that back (@serialize and
// @block, 2026-10-23), so the counter stays above every id loaded this
// session, a restart included.
//
// Duplicate detection: when REAPER copies an FX (Ctrl+drag, paste), the
// new instance inherits the source's slider4 unchanged — the `slider4 < 1`
// gate below misses this case. So we ALSO scan the instance registry: if
// any other slot reports our id with a recent heartbeat, we know we're a
// duplicate and mint a fresh id from the counter. The original instance
// keeps its id; the copy gets a new one. (Constants are defined below in
// the gmem layout section, but @init runs in source order — we forward-
// reference here as the JSFX compiler resolves @init names lazily.)
//
// Note: the registry base (GS_INST_REG_BASE = 2556, stride 4, 16 slots →
// 2556..2619) + the 3-second timeout are baked literally here so this
// collision check works even if a freshly-loaded chunk has not yet
// executed the constant-assignment block further down.
_init_collision = 0;
slider4 >= 1 ? (
  _init_si = 0;
  loop(16,
    _init_id = gmem[2556 + _init_si * 4];
    _init_hb = gmem[2556 + _init_si * 4 + 1];
    (_init_id == slider4 && _init_hb > 0 &&
     (time_precise() - _init_hb) < 3.0) ? _init_collision = 1;
    _init_si += 1;
  );
);
// ⚠️⚠️ MEASURED 2026-10-23 (EON_Probe_G1 leg F, REAPER 7.82): this @init runs
// BEFORE REAPER restores the saved slider -- on a project reopen and on an FX
// brought back online alike, `instance_id` (the named slider4) reads 0 here,
// and `slider4` is a separate plain variable that is ALWAYS 0 at a fresh @init.
// So this block mints on every load (the counter +1 per instance, whatever the
// ids are) and the saved id lands in instance_id afterwards (first seen at the
// @serialize read). The counter is raised from the RESTORED id there and every
// @block (H11: search `the new-id counter follows`); a raise here could never
// see it. (The collision scan above is the same: slider4 is 0, it never runs;
// copies are told apart by the @block duel.)
(slider4 < 1 || _init_collision) ? (
  // KIT_GMEM_INSTANCE_NEXT is defined later in @init (line ~540); JSFX
  // runs @init sequentially so by name resolution would silently use 0
  // here, which is KIT_GMEM_CMD — corrupting the bridge command channel
  // and giving every fresh instance a "random" id read back from CMD.
  // Use the literal slot 94 to bypass the variable-not-yet-assigned trap.
  gmem[94] += 1;
  slider4 = gmem[94];
);
instance_id = slider4;
_init_collision = _init_si = _init_id = _init_hb = 0;  // tidy locals
_reg_my_slot = -1;  // -1 = registry slot not yet claimed; @block claims on first run
_id64_slot = -1;    // the all-bank identity bands' last published slot: -1 = publish whole on the next block (a fresh claim, a sample-rate change)
_reg_try = 0;       // pending @block claim: slot + 1 (0 = none); see swing_registry_claim

// Patchbay loopback consumer state. patch_live is the AND of "the user asked
// for it" and "a Patchbay is actually alive out there" — the second half is
// what stops a deleted or mis-placed Patchbay from silently muting every pad.
patch_live      = 0;
_patch_rpos     = 0;
_patch_hb_prev  = -1;
_patch_hb_stall = PATCH_HB_STALL_MAX;   // assume dead until proven otherwise
_patch_lat      = 0;   // the loopback's latency in frames: the longest block since the aim (0 = not aimed yet)
_patch_base     = -1;   // impossible base: forces the slot-change reset on first claim
_patch_on_seen  = -1;   // -1 = not yet observed; the first @block only records, never acts
// Cursor re-aim (2026-09-11, see PATCH_OFF_GEN in rk_swing_patchbay.jsfx-inc).
patch_drain     = 0;    // patch_live AND the cursor is known good: what @sample reads on
_patch_gen_seen = -1;   // last producer incarnation observed (-1 = none yet)
_patch_live_prev = 0;   // to catch our own draining resuming after any gap
_patch_prime    = 0;    // 2 = hold this block, 1 = aim at WPOS and drain, 0 = steady
// Outputs step 5: the ring's layout, read from the Patchbay's NCH cell every block (rk_swing_patchbay CHANNEL LAYOUT).
patch_v2        = 0;    // 1 = the new layout: the bank and split pairs on 38..63, the bank pairs' sends on 34..37
patch_cols_live = PATCH_PCOLS_V1; patch_stride = PATCH_CHANS_V1; patch_depth = PATCH_FRAMES_V1;   // what the drain walks
_patch_layout_chg = 0;  // the layout changed since the last re-aim
_pdc_top_applied = 2;   // the PDC channel claim in force (2 = REAPER's resting claim while nothing is declared)

_last_block_time = time_precise();  // gap detector init (prevents false flush on first block)

// EON_DIAG counters (constants + layout at EON_DIAG_BASE below). ext_noinit
// keeps these one-shot per instance; a probe zeroes them through RESET_GEN.
diag_armed = 0; diag_t0 = 0; diag_t0_prev = 0; diag_t1 = 0; diag_spl = 0;
diag_blocks = 0; diag_stall_n = 0; diag_pause_n = 0; diag_gap_max = 0;
diag_cost_last = 0; diag_cost_max = 0; diag_cost_ema = 0; diag_ratio_max = 0;
diag_overrun_n = 0; diag_reset_seen = 0;
diag_ts = 0; diag_bema = 0; diag_sema = 0;   // first-@sample stamp; @block / @sample split EMAs
diag_p87_t0 = 0; diag_p87_last = 0;          // +15: the CMD-87 path publish's own wall time

// LCD banner state (rk_swing_ui_state, 2026-09-08): bridge heartbeat AGE tracking
// (-1 = no value seen yet, so the first frame counts as movement and never
// flashes the banner), the registry-full latch, and the session-volatile
// dismiss flags (deliberately not serialized).
_hb_seen = -1; _hb_seen_t = time_precise(); _hb_stale = 0;
_regfull_since = 0; _regfull_dismissed = 0; _ext_dismissed = 0;
_oldbr_dismissed = 0;  // "Kit Bridge is out of date" banner, session-volatile like the two
                       // above. Re-armed by a click on the greyed WIRED button, so the one
                       // control the skew actually breaks can always summon its own reason.

// ─── Constants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NUM_PADS    = 16;
MAX_VOICES  = 128;      // Pad banks step 2c (Spec_Swing_Pad_Banks 10): a pad can put five things in the air; behind v_hi the @sample loop pays only for live voices.
                        // 48 -> 128 on 2026-10-14 (Spec_Swing_Seq_View decision 17, phase V): the sequencer's chords need the room. The pool's
                        // SIZE costs nothing (measured: a 48 and a 128 pool read alike at equal counts); each SOUNDING voice ~59 us per 1024
                        // block after the voice loop's speed job (was ~83), 128 voices at once ~44 % of the block on the user's PC with no late
                        // blocks; ~33 K more cells (v_* and the SYN state) against the ~5 M headroom. Voices are never serialized.
STEAL_FADES = 4;        // steal-fade slots past the pool: a stolen voice fades out in one of them (A-2)
V_SLOTS     = MAX_VOICES + STEAL_FADES;   // every v_* array, and every kill / release loop, runs to here
SLOT_SIZE   = 4000000;
NUM_BANKS   = 4;        // Pad banks (Spec_Swing_Pad_Banks): resident kits per instance, A..D. NUM_PADS stays "pads per bank" (every UI loop).
NUM_SLOTS   = NUM_BANKS * NUM_PADS;   // absolute pad slots (bank * NUM_PADS + pad): every per-pad ENGINE array and loop is this wide (step 2b)
// Output pairs (Pad Banks Outputs step 1; swing_out_pair in rk_swing_alloc): 0..15 bank A's pads, 16..18 the
// Verb / Delay / Smash returns, then the bank B, C, D tracks and ten split-off pairs, 32 pairs = the 64 pins.
OUT_PAIR_BANK  = 19;   // = PATCH_PAIR_HI in rk_swing_patchbay (the Wired ring's columns): keep the two equal
OUT_PAIR_SPLIT = 22;
OUT_PAIRS      = 32;
OUT_CH_BASE    = 38;    // the channels multi-out clears / guards / crossfades while no awake pad plays above them
// bank_cur: the bank on screen (UI state; step 4 wires the strip). SERIALIZED at ser_ver 76 (step 3a), so it
// is assigned NOWHERE in @init -- the zero-default rule every serialized scalar follows (an @init assignment
// would stamp 0 back over a restored value when @init runs after @serialize). swing_bp(i) = bank_cur * NUM_PADS + i.
SEND_FX_RESERVE = 19000000; // cells kept above the pool for the send FX, the Anvil tables, the swap chunk and the undo slot (~1.2-1.4M by the inits' constants plus the 16M undo backup; asserted below). On a machine whose backed top is lower than the layout, the FX base moves down to (backed top - reserve) and the pool ends there: a short machine loses pool, never the FX or undo.
AUDIO_AREA  = 104000000;   // the pad-audio pool above s_audio_start, shared by every slot: ~20 min of stereo at 44.1k, 26 full pads (or 6 pads carrying four 45 s layers). Was NUM_PADS * SLOT_SIZE (64M) until 2026-09-23, 116M for an hour before the undo backup grew with the layers; the 128M grant is backed (f87d688c) and the startup self-check below lowers the pool on a machine that cannot back it.
STORE_RATE_MAX = 48000; // Sample storage-rate ceiling on the NO-BRIDGE file path (Spec_Swing_Pad_Banks §5.5): a file above it is read through file_riff's 'rqsr' request and lands at this rate. Every bridge route honours the user's Store setting (48k / 96k / native); this fallback keeps the default.
SWAP_CHUNK  = 16384;    // pad-swap scratch (cells): swap_pads() moves audio through ONE chunk, never a whole slot
// Sliced sample loader (rk_swing_core swing_ldr_*): cells of load work per
// @block, scaled from samplesblock so a slice costs ~12% of a block at 48k.
// The max is half of EEL2's 2^20 loop cap — every slice loop stays under it.
LDR_CELLS_PER_SPL = 256;
LDR_BUDGET_MIN    = 16384;
LDR_BUDGET_MAX    = 524288;
LDR_JOB_STRIDE    = 256;    // cells per loader job record (fields + 200-cell RMS scratch)
// Sliced undo capture (udo_cow_upto, rk_drumkit_dsp): cells of BACKUP copy per
// @block. memcpy runs ~350 cells/us here, so 384 cells per sample of block is
// ~5% of the period at every buffer size (24 576 at 64, 98 304 at 256, 393 216
// at 1024) -- a whole 4 M-cell slot saves in ~40 blocks instead of one stall; a
// four-layer 45 s pad (16M, since 2026-09-23) in ~160.
UDO_COW_PER_SPL   = 384;
UDO_COW_MIN       = 24576;
UDO_COW_MAX       = 393216;
WV_RES      = 256;      // waveform cache points (higher = smoother LCD waveform)
KS          = 16;       // knob memory slots
SILENCE_T   = 10;
END_FADE    = 256;
DENORM_THR  = 0.00000000000000000001;  // 1e-20
BUS_TAIL_FLOOR = 0.000001;  // -120 dBFS: a send bus switched OFF is considered
                            // finished once its wet sits under this. Far above
                            // DENORM_THR on purpose - denorm is "the number is
                            // garbage", this is "the tail is inaudible".
DBL_CLICK_T = 0.35;     // double-click detection window (seconds)
MAX_LAYERS  = 4;
LAYER_SIZE  = SLOT_SIZE;   // a layer holds what a pad holds (user, 2026-09-23): 45 s stereo at 44.1k. Was SLOT_SIZE / MAX_LAYERS = 1,000,000 (11 s) while four layers had to share one fixed slot; per-layer regions (rk_swing_alloc) freed them.
UDO_VSLOT   = MAX_LAYERS * LAYER_SIZE;   // the command-undo backup's VIRTUAL slot: a plain pad at [0, SLOT_SIZE), layer l at [l * LAYER_SIZE, ...) -- one pad's worst case, 16M cells
LPATH_STR_BASE = 200;   // string slot base for layer paths: 200..455 (NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS = 256 slots since step 2b)
// Step 3a (2026-09-23): the per-pad name / path / custom-name strings are NUMBERED slots too -- sixty-four
// named strings (#pn0..#pn63 x3) would have been a 192-way ternary. get_name_slot / get_path_slot /
// get_cname_slot (rk_swing_core) add the pad to these. Numbered slots start empty, like named ones.
// #idn0..15 (the IDENT publish's last-written names, rk_swing_core) stay named and sixteen wide: that
// band publishes the ACTIVE bank (spec 9, step 5).
PNAME_STR_BASE = 456;   // 456..519  pad display names
PPATH_STR_BASE = 520;   // 520..583  pad-main sample paths
CNAME_STR_BASE = 584;   // 584..647  custom names (the user's rename)
BKNAME_STR_BASE = 648;  // 648..651  the four BANK names (step 4b, ser_ver 77): a kit loaded into a bank names that bank
ID64NAME_STR_BASE = 652; // 652..715  the all-bank identity publish's last-written names (its shadows; get_id64name_slot, 2026-10-22)
BANK_STRIP_H = 26;      // the bank strip above the pad grid, in design px (step 4b; Spec_Swing_Pad_Banks 8, mockup frame 1)

// ── No-embed save policy (Phase 4, ser_ver 51) ────────────────────────────
// embed_mode (serialized, default AUTO) picks how @serialize persists kit
// audio: AUTO writes a disk-marker whenever the bridge has verified a project
// sidecar this minute (any size), else embeds under the threshold and markers
// above it; ALWAYS embeds up to the hard cap (else marker+warn); NEVER always
// markers. The recoverability floor overrides every mode (see @serialize).
// Ceiling measured 2026-07-14: REAPER truncates the JSFX @serialize blob at
// 32 MiB (= 8,387,609 interleaved samples, 4 B/sample). See
// Spec_Swing_PerPad_Sidecar_Load.md §4.
EMBED_MODE_AUTO   = 0;
EMBED_MODE_ALWAYS = 1;
EMBED_MODE_NEVER  = 2;
EMBED_CAP_SAMPLES    = 8387609;  // hard truncation cliff (32 MiB / 4 B)
EMBED_AUTO_SAMPLES   = 6291456;  // AUTO switch-to-marker threshold WITHOUT a verified sidecar (24 MiB / 4 B, 75% of cap)

// ─── Memory layout ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
freemem = 0;

p_gain      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_pan       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_tune      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // ±24 semitones
p_attack    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // ms
p_decay     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // ms
p_sustain   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 0–1
p_release   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // ms
p_adsr_user = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 1 = user has manually tuned ADSR (skip analyze_adsr on drag-in)
p_mute      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_solo      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_note      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_output    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // the output CHOSEN (0-15 bank A's pairs, then the bank
                                             // tracks and split pairs); swing_out_pair says where it
                                             // plays -- never read it raw for routing or a label
p_note_lock = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 0 = follows root_note + slot; 1 = the user's note (MIDI learn, a pin, a drag, set-note); 2 = a MAP preset's or a nudge's note (survives recalcs; a later preset replaces it -- Pad Banks audit S9)
// ver 50: per-pad chromatic key RANGE, stored as SEMITONE OFFSETS from the
// pad's root note (p_note). p_rng_lo = semis below root, p_rng_hi = semis
// above (both >= 0). Effective key range = [p_note - p_rng_lo, p_note +
// p_rng_hi]. Default 0/0 = single-note pad (a drum — today's behavior).
// lo|hi > 0 = chromatic pad: any note in range triggers it, pitched by
// (played - p_note) semitones. Storing OFFSETS (not absolute lo/hi) means the
// range auto-follows every p_note change (MAP presets, root shift, mapping
// drags, MIDI learn) with no edits to those sites — one source of truth.
p_rng_lo    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // semitones below root (>= 0)
p_rng_hi    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // semitones above root (>= 0)
p_panL      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // precomputed pan left
p_panR      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // precomputed pan right

// ─── Swing Pitch (Part B) per-pad state ────────────────────────────────
// User-facing mode + algo choice per pad. Default 0 = Repitch (today's
// behavior — local SincResampler, zero latency). Shadow arrays track the
// last value written to gmem so @block only fires atomic_set on actual
// change — keeps the bus quiet when nothing's moving.
sp_pitch_mode        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;   // 0=Repitch 1=Tuned 2=Stretch
sp_pitch_algo        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;   // 0=Drum 1=Tonal 2=Texture 3=Voice
// Tune (semitones) the current Tuned-mode buffer is baked at. Voices play a
// RESIDUAL (p_tune - this) so a knob move responds INSTANTLY via varispeed
// while the duration-preserving bake catches up (set to p_tune by the CMD-65/67
// swap). _baked_tune_synced: one-shot latch — sync sp_baked_tune to p_tune on
// the first @block after load (the restored buffer is baked at the saved tune).
// PER-LAYER (A4/A5): a layered pad bakes EACH non-empty layer independently
// (Sum/VelSplit/RR all sound layers 1+), so the baked-tune anchor is keyed by
// (pad,layer) = pad*MAX_LAYERS + layer. Layer 0 / non-layered pads use index
// pad*MAX_LAYERS + 0. The residual in launch_voices_for_pad indexes by the
// selected layer so each layer plays duration-preserved at its own baked tune.
sp_baked_tune        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;
_baked_tune_synced   = 0;
// Per-pad SOURCE GENERATION counter. Bumped whenever a pad's audio changes by
// any JSFX-side route (load_from_path / load_layer_from_path / clear_layer) —
// drag-drop onto the grid or overlay, browser load, or pad clear. Blast-
// published to gmem (STRETCH_PER_PAD_SRCGEN_BASE) every @block so the Kit
// Bridge can detect the change and invalidate the Extension's cached bake/
// preload source for that pad (the Extension keys its decode cache on the
// published temp-WAV path, which is otherwise stable across a sample swap →
// a Tuned/Stretch pad would resurrect the OLD sample on mode switch).
sp_src_gen           = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
memset(sp_src_gen, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
// The pitch SPOT map (Plan_Swing_Pad_Banks_Tuned §5, §5A.5; step 3, 2026-10-05): the Extension's sixteen rows
// per instance are SPOTS a pad holds. pr_pad[spot] = its pad (-1 free), sp_row[pad] = its spot (-1 none);
// derived at @init (swing_spot_init: identity, bank A pad s on spot s), never serialized, no ser_ver.
// sp_pub_gen[spot] = the source generation the handshake has RELEASED to the SRCGEN band; sp_map_gen[spot] =
// the one the map last published; sp_hold[pad] / sp_hold_hb[pad] = the Stretch hold and the heartbeat it ends
// at (rk_swing_block_pitch swing_spot_tick). The rows are sixteen wide, the per-pad ones NUM_SLOTS.
// Step 4 (2026-10-09): spots are LENT to pads of any bank (swing_spot_assign); pr_state[spot] = SPOT_STATE_*.
pr_pad               = freemem; freemem += NUM_PADS;    // sixteen: the spots
pr_state             = freemem; freemem += NUM_PADS;    // sixteen: the spots
pr_drain             = freemem; freemem += NUM_PADS;    // sixteen: the spots' drain token (epoch + a count; in the map's STATE cell)
sp_pub_gen           = freemem; freemem += NUM_PADS;    // sixteen: the spots
sp_map_gen           = freemem; freemem += NUM_PADS;    // sixteen: the spots
sp_row               = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sp_hold              = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sp_hold_hb           = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
memset(sp_hold, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
memset(sp_hold_hb, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
// The pad-swap queue (2026-10-12): swap_pads (@gfx) posts one cell per swap, a * NUM_SLOTS + b, then bumps
// sp_swap_req; swing_spot_tick (@block, the spot map's one writer) applies every swap in order. One cell per swap,
// so a second swap before @block runs (Swing bypassed, the engine stalled) no longer replaces the first, and one
// store per swap, so a pair is never read half old. Only cells below sp_swap_req are read: no memset.
SP_SWAP_QN           = 64;
sp_swap_q            = freemem; freemem += SP_SWAP_QN;
// Preserve-live kit reload (project open / audio repair): 1 = this pad already
// holds audio (or is deliberately empty) after @serialize, so the kit file the
// bridge is re-staging must not touch it -- only blank casualties take the
// kit's copy. Decided per import in rk_swing_ui_state (state 2), read by the
// META sweep and every state-3 audio path. Found live 2026-09-08: a pad the
// user replaced came back as the kit's original on the next real project open.
kit_keep_pad         = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
memset(kit_keep_pad, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
// v3 stateless protocol: the JSFX no longer diffs — swing_block_pitch_tick
// blast-publishes mode/tune/algo every tick and the Extension owns all diff
// state. The former sp_pitch_*_shadow arrays are gone.
// Step 3b: per-pad monotonic trigger counter. Incremented in
// launch_voices_for_pad when the target pad is in Mode=Stretch; the
// counter value is atomic_set'd into the STRETCH_PER_PAD_TRIGGER gmem
// band so the Extension's audio_hook can detect new triggers by diff'ing
// against its per-pad shadow.
sp_pitch_trigger_cnt = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
// Step 3b: per-pad read cursor for the Stretch SPSC ring. JSFX writes
// these via atomic_set in @sample (after consuming a stereo frame);
// the Extension audio_hook reads them via atomic_get to know how many
// frames the consumer has caught up on. Initialized to 0 (= empty ring
// at startup, perfectly aligned with the Extension's also-zero write_pos).
stretch_read_pos     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
stretch_hold         = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // sub-block start offset, in samples
stretch_choked       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // A-7: 0 sounding, 1 choked and fading, 2 parked (ring discarded)
stretch_gain         = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // A-7: the drain's gain, 1 until choked
i = 0; loop(NUM_SLOTS, stretch_gain[i] = 1; i += 1;);

p_att_c     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // precomputed coefficients
p_dec_c     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_rel_c     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_inc_base  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // pitch increment

s_len       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
s_start     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
s_end       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
s_skip      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
s_norm      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
s_norm_gain = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
s_dirty     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
s_sr        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // source sample rate
// Pad-audio regions (banks step 1a pointers, step 2a allocator; Spec_Swing_Pad_Banks 4.2 /
// 5.3): every reader takes a slot's address from here, never from s_audio_start plus
// pad * SLOT_SIZE. A slot holds a PLAIN region (p_aptr / p_alen) or per-layer regions
// (p_lptr / p_llen), each carved from the area by rk_swing_alloc at load time; len 0 = no
// region, ptr -1. Layers are NOT contiguous any more: the command-undo backup keeps the old
// slot layout as a VIRTUAL slot and maps through swing_slot_v2p_t (rk_swing_alloc).
p_aptr      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;               // plain region: audio start (absolute cell) per slot, -1 = none
p_alen      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;               // plain region: cells allocated (0 = none); the loader's pad-main cap
p_lptr      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // layer regions: audio start per layer, -1 = none
p_llen      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // layer regions: cells allocated per layer (0 = none)
// Allocator scratch (rk_swing_alloc): the undo capture's region snapshot (one pad's five
// regions, ptr + len) that every backup copy reads through, and two displaced lists for the
// one-shot callers that free at once -- @block's (kit hot-swap, bakes, the layer copy) and
// @serialize's (the embed read). A loader job carries its own list inside its record.
udo_s2_srcp = freemem; freemem += MAX_LAYERS + 1;
udo_s2_srcl = freemem; freemem += MAX_LAYERS + 1;
_al_dl_blk  = freemem; freemem += 2 * (MAX_LAYERS + 1);
_al_dl_srz  = freemem; freemem += 2 * (MAX_LAYERS + 1);

// Per-layer metadata (NUM_PADS * MAX_LAYERS = 64 entries each)
l_len       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // sample length per layer (0 = empty)
l_start     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // start trim 0-1
l_end       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // end trim 0-1
l_sr        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // source sample rate
l_norm      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // normalize enable
l_norm_gain = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // normalization gain
l_vel_lo    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // velocity split low threshold 0-1
l_vel_hi    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // velocity split high threshold 0-1
l_rr_order  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // round-robin play order (0-based)
l_gain      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;  // per-layer gain (0.0–2.0, 1.0=unity)

// Per-pad layer control arrays
p_layer_cnt = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // number of loaded layers (1-4, 0=legacy single)
p_layer_mode= freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 0=single, 1=vel-split, 2=round-robin, 3=sum
p_rr_idx    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // round-robin index counter
p_sum_tight = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // sum tightness: 0.0=tight, 1.0=loose
p_rpt_div   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad repeat division (0=OFF/follow global)
p_rpt_ctr   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad repeat sample counter
p_rpt_swph  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad repeat swing phase
p_rpt_hold  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad samples held (grid-entry guard)
p_sample_offset = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad sample offset 0-1
_blk_trig   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad dedup: already triggered this @block
_blk_off    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // note-off received this @block
_blk_last_off = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 1 if the pad's LAST midi event this @block was a note-off (order, not just presence)
_blk_trig_ofs = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // in-block sample offset of the pad's latest MIDI trigger; read only while _blk_trig is set
// The voice schedule (swing_voice_choke_at / swing_voice_release_at, rk_swing_core): what a MIDI
// event does to the voices already sounding happens AT the event's sample, from @sample -- a hit
// inside the block runs its choke / duplicate-kill pass there, and a gate-mode note-off
// releases its voices there. Kept in offset order; a full schedule acts at once.
// ckq_pad = the pad of a choke pass, or -1 - voice for a release; ckq_gen = that voice's
// v_gen when the note-off read it. 128: a note-off can name several voices (layers + SYN).
// With _blk_trig_ofs and v_gen: about 500 cells below s_audio_start, against the HEADROOM
// BUDGET (~5M), noted, like the meq_cv cells.
CKQ_MAX  = 128;
ckq_pad  = freemem; freemem += CKQ_MAX;
ckq_ofs  = freemem; freemem += CKQ_MAX;
ckq_gen  = freemem; freemem += CKQ_MAX;
ckq_n = 0; ckq_i = 0; ckq_spl = 0;
_retrig_cd  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad retrigger cooldown (samples remaining)
_mute_eff_prev = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // effective mute (own M, or someone else's S) as of the last @block; the 0->1 edge silences the pad
v_pos       = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;
v_slot      = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;
v_gain      = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;
v_note      = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;
v_inc       = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;
v_age       = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;
v_env       = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;
v_stage     = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // 1=atk 2=dec 3=sus 4=rel
v_startpos  = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // saved start pos for loose sum timing
v_decay_ct  = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;
v_sg        = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // sample gain (norm or pad gain)
v_layer     = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // which layer the voice is playing
v_fastrel   = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // 1 = release under steal_coeff as well: a pad muted while sounding (swing_voice_silence_pad)
v_quiet     = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // SYN: consecutive samples
                                                   // the engine has been silent
v_gen       = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // bumped at every voice start: a queued note-off release
                                            // names (voice, generation), so a slot reused since is left alone

// ─── SYN slot: per-pad synth layer (Spec_Swing_Synth_Layer §2) ────────────
// ser_ver 52 block. Macros live as 8 SEPARATE per-pad arrays (undo/swap/
// serialize symmetry with every other p_* field); gathered into a contiguous
// 8-cell scratch at trigger time for the rk_syn_* API.
ps_enable   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;   // 0=off (default), 1=on
ps_engine   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;   // family + 10*type (0..38): family =
                                              // engine%10 (0..8, RK_SYN_FAMILIES),
                                              // type = floor(engine/10) (0..3).
                                              // NEVER compare raw — decode with %10
                                              // (a raw read is exactly the bug the
                                              // SYN chip shipped with).
ps_level    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;   // 0..2, default 1
ps_vel_lo   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;   // vel-split participation
ps_vel_hi   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
ps_rr_order = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;   // RR position (default MAX_LAYERS = after samples)
ps_mac0 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
ps_mac1 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
ps_mac2 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
ps_mac3 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
ps_mac4 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
ps_mac5 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
ps_mac6 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
ps_mac7 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
v_kind      = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;                       // 0=sample, 1=synth
// 1 = this voice is a STRETCH pad playing LOCALLY because the Extension could not
// be reached (no registry slot). Per VOICE, not per pad, for the same reason
// v_kind is: the pad can claim a slot while this note is still ringing, and the
// note must not fall silent underneath the player when it does.
v_stfb      = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;
// The voice's block constants (phase V of Spec_Swing_Seq_View, 2026-10-14): what the @sample voice loop
// used to resolve from the pad and layer tables EVERY sample -- the buffer pointer, the interleaved
// start / end positions and the Stretch sum gate -- set by swing_voice_prep (rk_swing_core) at launch,
// when a stolen voice is parked, and for every live voice at the top of @block's voice pass. The
// loop's bookkeeping was ~52 % of a sounding voice's cost (handoff Swing_Voice_Loop_Cost_Split).
v_bptr      = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // buffer pointer (p_aptr or p_lptr of the voice's layer)
v_astart    = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // interleaved start position (trim)
v_aend      = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // interleaved end position (trim) - SILENCE_T
v_sum       = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS;  // 1 = sums into its pad (SYN, a Stretch fallback, a B..D pad, a non-Stretch pad)
v_syn_state = freemem; freemem += V_SLOTS * RK_SYN_STATE_SIZE; // per-voice engine state
_syn_mac_scratch = freemem; freemem += RK_SYN_MACROS;                   // trigger-time gather
freemem = rk_syn_init(freemem);                                         // engine LUTs (once)
freemem = swing_drum3d_init(freemem);                                   // SYN panel 3D meshes
freemem = swing_synprev_init(freemem);  // pad editor's synth voice preview

// ─── Kit-macro tables (slice 1, Spec_Swing_Macro_System §2) ──────────────
// Session-volatile until the ser_ver 54 gate lands (slice 5). STATIC
// bounds: KMAC_N macros × KMAC_MAX_MAP mappings each. kmac_pad: -2 = every
// pad of all four banks, -1 = selected pad (any bank), 0..NUM_SLOTS-1 an
// absolute pad (Pad Banks, 2026-09-24). kmac_curve: shape exponent
// (1 = linear), negative = inverted response at |curve|. Engine =
// kmac_tick() in @block, applying through swing_fx_set (value + recalc,
// NEVER mark_dirty — macro motion is performance, not an edit; spec §3).
// ⚠️ These are KIT macros — unrelated to the synth layer's per-pad
// ps_mac0..7 above, which are DD-101 engine knobs.
KMAC_N       = 8;
KMAC_MAX_MAP = 8;
KMAC_NSNAP   = 4;              // snapshot slots I..IV (spec §4; room for 8 later)
// Virtual CORE-param pids (2026-08-21): macro targets beyond the FX_PID_*
// vocabulary — pad tune / pan / envelope, the params WIDTH·PITCH·DECAY
// presets need. 100+ stays clear of real pids (0..27) and the bus range
// (64..75); these NEVER touch the strip publish band (its layout is pid-
// indexed 0..31) and they are core VOICE params, so they stay audible in
// multi-out takeover (the strips carry FX only).
// Kit-transfer band (flat, CMD-serialized kit window): +0 = bridge→JSFX
// staged flag · +1 model ver · +2..9 values · +10..17 nmap · +18..25 scope
// · +26..33 color · +34..97 pad · +98..161 pid · +162..225 lo · +226..289
// hi · +290..353 curve · +354..385 snap · +386..389 snap_has · +390
// snap_act · +391..486 names (v2) · +487..494 FULL mapping counts (v3: the
// bank B..D mappings sit after the old-safe ones and +10..17 counts only
// the old-safe ones, so a pre-banks reader never lands a B..D mapping on
// pad 16). Publisher = ui_state export phase; consumer = ui_state kit
// adopt; bridge packs/stages it as v4 tail tag 2. MUST match
// Swing_Kit_Bridge.lua eon_kmac_pack/eon_kmac_stage and the gmem map.
KMAC_KIT_BASE = 26090640;
// S3c (2026-10-20): the step sequencer's kit record band (rk_seq_core seq_kit_publish / seq_kit_adopt; the bridge's
// eon_seq_pack / eon_seq_stage pack it as v4 tail tag 7). +0 the staged flag, +1 version, +2 cells, +3 the overflow
// when refused, +8.. the tagged stream (SONG, PATTERNS, NOTES), EON_SEQ_KIT_CAP cells at most. MUST match the bridge
// and .refs/gmem_regions_supplement.tsv.
EON_SEQ_KIT_BASE = 31400000;
EON_SEQ_KIT_CAP  = 65536;
// S6 (2026-10-21): the step sequencer's PRINT mailbox (rk_seq_core seq_print_run; the bridge's cmd 96 / eon_seq_print_build,
// and cmd 53 / eon_seq_song_build for the song -- 97 until the small-things round, now the bridge's "dialog open" park only):
// +0 state (0 idle, 1 the bridge wrote the span, 2 the plugin wrote the hits), +1 the start beat, +2 the beats, +3 the
// hits, +4 the pattern, +5 cut, +8.. the hits x SEQ_PRINT_F. MUST match the bridge and the supplement.
EON_SEQ_PRINT_BASE = 31470000;
EON_SEQ_PRINT_CAP  = 13107;
// The small-things round (2026-10-23; READ_HIGH_MEDIUM:159): the band is ONE for every Swing, so every instance saw
// state 1 and walked its own pattern into it -- with two Swings the print could hold the other one's. The bridge
// writes the requesting instance's id here BEFORE it raises the state to 1 (CMD 96 / 53: kept from LOCK when the
// command arrives); only that instance walks (rk_seq_core seq_block_tick). Past the last hit cell (+65542), inside the
// declared band (through +65551). An older bridge (GS_BRIDGE_LEVEL under BRIDGE_LEVEL_PRINT_OWNER) never writes it:
// the plugin then walks on state 1 alone, as before the round.
EON_SEQ_PRINT_OWNER = EON_SEQ_PRINT_BASE + 65544;
KMAC_PID_CORE_BASE = 100;
KMAC_PID_TUNE   = 100;   // p_tune  ±24 semis  → recalc_pad
KMAC_PID_PAN    = 101;   // p_pan   -1..1      → p_panL/p_panR (no recalc)
KMAC_PID_DECAY  = 102;   // p_decay 1..2000 ms → recalc_pad
KMAC_PID_ATTACK = 103;   // p_attack 0..500 ms → recalc_pad
// The pad's OWN DD-101 engine knobs (ps_mac0..7), +0..+7. Which knob each
// index means depends on the pad's FAMILY — kick 2 is A.DEC, everything
// else's 1 is DECAY — so surfaces label them via _syn_macro_label(engine, k)
// rather than a fixed table.
//
// ⭐ WHY THESE EXIST: a synth pad's real decay lives here and NOWHERE else.
// The pad ADSR (KMAC_PID_DECAY) can only ever ATTENUATE what the engine
// already rendered, and its decay stage is exponential — measured against the
// engine's own envelope it costs a long voice a third to a half of its tail
// before a knob is even touched (8T8's SUB: 55% left at the range maximum).
// Writing the engine knob instead is inert at rest and goes BOTH directions.
// ⛔ Do not "simplify" a synth DECAY macro back onto the pad ADSR.
KMAC_PID_SYN_BASE = 110;
KMAC_PID_SYN_N    = 8;
KMAC_NAME_LEN   = 12;    // custom macro-name cap (kit block v2 char cells)
// Last-touched assign target (editor "+ LAST" + right-click menus): set by
// swing_fx_apply (PadFX panel / strip / viewer edits) and the LCD PAD-tab
// TUNE/PAN knobs. -1 = nothing touched yet this session.
kmac_lt_pad = -1;
kmac_lt_pid = -1;
kmac_lt_t   = 0;
// sliderchange mask covering the 8 macro sliders (32..39 = bits 31..38).
// Pow arithmetic, never (1<<n) — these bits sit past the 32-bit shift range
// (feedback_eel2_shift_32bit).
KMAC_SLMASK  = 2^39 - 2^31;
kmac_nmap  = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N;
kmac_scope = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N;                 // reserved (per-mapping -1 covers PAD-follow in v1)
kmac_color = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N;                 // identity palette idx (UI slice)
kmac_val   = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N;                 // gathered slider values (@block)
kmac_last  = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N;                 // change detection (@block)
kmac_pad   = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N * KMAC_MAX_MAP;
kmac_pid   = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N * KMAC_MAX_MAP;
kmac_lo    = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N * KMAC_MAX_MAP;
kmac_hi    = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N * KMAC_MAX_MAP;
kmac_curve = freemem; freemem += KMAC_N * KMAC_MAX_MAP;
kmac_snap     = freemem; freemem += KMAC_NSNAP * KMAC_N;  // snapshot values, slot*8+k
kmac_snap_has = freemem; freemem += KMAC_NSNAP;           // 1 = slot captured (empty
                                                          // slots never recall/morph)
// kmac_snap_act (armed snapshot slot) is SERIALIZED at ser_ver 54 — no
// @init assignment (EEL2 zero-init covers fresh instances; the serialize
// rule bars @init resets of serialized scalars).
kmac_primed = 0;
kmac_force  = 0;
// Recalc owed per pad by the macro pass, as bits (1 = fx, 2 = pad). Written
// and cleared ONLY inside kmac_tick/kmac_apply, both @block -- deliberately
// not a "defer recalc" flag on swing_fx_set, which @gfx also calls: a shared
// flag would let a UI edit landing mid-pass have its recalc swallowed.
kmac_rcp = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
// The UI thread's own recalc requests (A-9a): per-pad request counters written
// only by @gfx (swing_rcp_post_* in rk_drumkit_dsp) and done counters written
// only by @block (swing_block_rcp_settle in rk_swing_block); a difference is a
// pending recalc. The two scalars cover the master comp and the master chain.
_rcp_req_fx   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
_rcp_req_pad  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
_rcp_done_fx  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
_rcp_done_pad = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
memset(_rcp_req_fx, 0, NUM_SLOTS); memset(_rcp_req_pad, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
memset(_rcp_done_fx, 0, NUM_SLOTS); memset(_rcp_done_pad, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
_rcp_req_cmp = 0; _rcp_done_cmp = 0; _rcp_req_master = 0; _rcp_done_master = 0;
// Pad clicks and gate-mode releases from the UI thread (A-9b): two single-writer
// rings. The UI appends (swing_gt_post / swing_gt_post_release in rk_drumkit_dsp,
// the write index bumped LAST) and @block consumes (swing_block_gt_consume beside
// the bridge's trigger, swing_block_gt_release at the block's end). Both indexes
// only grow; wr - rd is the pending count, and a full ring drops the click rather
// than overwrite one in flight.
GT_RING = 16;
_gt_pad   = freemem; freemem += GT_RING;
_gt_note  = freemem; freemem += GT_RING;
_gt_vel   = freemem; freemem += GT_RING;
_gt_flash = freemem; freemem += GT_RING;
_gtr_pad  = freemem; freemem += GT_RING;
_gt_wr = 0; _gt_rd = 0; _gtr_wr = 0; _gtr_rd = 0;
// (Slice-1 test mapping is seeded further down in @init, AFTER the
// FX_PID_* constants are assigned — they are 0 at this point in the run.)

// Waveform thumbnail cache: WV_RES points per pad. Two caches for stereo
// display: wv_cache holds the L-channel sample at each step, wv_cache_R
// holds R. Mono files end up with identical L/R, so the pad display shows
// a symmetric waveform; stereo files show the L and R envelopes diverging
// (top half = |L|, bottom half = |R|). Both populated by build_wv_cache.
wv_cache    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * WV_RES;
wv_cache_R  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * WV_RES;

// Per-(pad,layer) waveform cache for the PAD-DETAIL OVERLAY only. The overlay
// draws the selected layer's LIVE buffer (for zoom), so a Tuned bake — which
// overwrites a layer buffer with pitched audio — moved the displayed waveform.
// This frozen cache is built ONLY on sample load (s_dirty in build_wv_cache),
// never on a bake, so the overview (unzoomed) detail view shows the ORIGINAL
// sample shape, matching the grid. Stored NORMALIZED (norm gain applied) like
// wv_cache; the zoomed detail view still reads the live buffer. Raw L / R.
ov_wv_cache   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS * WV_RES;
ov_wv_cache_R = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS * WV_RES;
// Per-(pad,layer) "overlay waveform captured" flag. build_wv_cache rebuilds a
// layer's ov_wv_cache from the buffer ONLY while the layer is still original
// (sp_baked_tune==0) OR has never been captured (=0, the reload fallback). Once
// a layer is baked, the frozen original is kept so a later s_dirty (offset/ADSR/
// gain knob) doesn't re-snapshot the pitched buffer and move the waveform.
// Re-armed (set 0) on layer load/clear. Persists across @init (no memset) so the
// captured original survives an SR-change re-init.
ov_cap        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;

// Knob memory: 7 knobs per pad (ATK/DEC/SUS/REL/GAIN/PAN/TUNE) + 1 global vol
KM_PER_PAD  = 8;
km_pads     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * KM_PER_PAD * KS;
km_gvol     = freemem; freemem += KS;
km_swing    = freemem; freemem += KS;  // swing amount knob memory

// Per-pad peak metering (written in @sample, read/reset in @gfx)
p_peak      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_peak_hold = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;

// Repeat: track which pads are held via MIDI
p_held      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_held_vel  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_held_note = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // played note of the held key (for tempo-repeat pitch on chromatic pads)
p_press     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // live channel/poly pressure under a held pad

// On-pad mini knobs: 2 per pad (VOL, PAN) — separate from overlay knobs
KM_PAD_MINI = 2;
km_pad_vol_pan = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * KM_PAD_MINI * KS;

// Per-pad color hue (0.0–1.0 float, used with HSL→RGB)
p_color     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;

// New per-pad controls: choke groups, one-shot, reverse
p_choke     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // choke group: 0=none, 1-8
p_oneshot   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 1 = one-shot (ignore note-off, play through)
p_reverse   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 1 = reverse playback
p_swapLR    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 1 = swap left/right channels at the pad accumulator
p_stereo    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 1 = source file was stereo (drives 2-waveform display); 0 = mono

// ─── Per-pad FX parameters ──────────────────────────────────────────────
fx_hpf_freq = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // HPF cutoff Hz (20–20000)
fx_lpf_freq = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // LPF cutoff Hz (20–20000)
fx_eq_lo    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ low  gain dB (-12..+12)
fx_eq_mid   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ mid  gain dB (-12..+12)
fx_eq_hi    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ high gain dB (-12..+12)
fx_eq_lo_freq  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ low frequency Hz (draggable, 40-500)
fx_eq_mid_freq = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ mid frequency Hz (draggable, 200-8000)
// v46: 4th EQ band — second bell ("hi-mid"), serialized at ser_ver >= 46
fx_eq_mid2      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ hi-mid gain dB (-12..+12)
fx_eq_mid2_freq = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ hi-mid frequency Hz (draggable, 500-12000)
fx_eq_mid_q     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ mid bell Q (wheel over node, 0.3-6, default 0.8)
fx_eq_mid2_q    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ hi-mid bell Q (wheel over node, 0.3-6, default 0.8)
// v48: per-band shelf Q (wheel over the Low/High nodes; 0.7071 == old S=1.0)
fx_eq_lo_q      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ low shelf Q (0.3-6, default 0.7071)
fx_eq_hi_q      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ high shelf Q (0.3-6, default 0.7071)
fx_eq_hi_freq  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // EQ high frequency Hz (draggable, 2000-16000)
fx_sat_drv  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Saturation drive (0–1)
fx_drv_mode = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Drive mode: 0=SOFT 1=TUBE 2=TAPE 3=FUZZ 4=CLIP
fx_bc_rate  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Bitcrush rate reduction (0=off, 1=max crush)
fx_bc_bits  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Bitcrush bit depth (16=clean, 1=destroyed)
fx_snd_dly  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Per-pad delay send amount (0–1)
fx_snd_rvb  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Per-pad reverb send amount (0–1)
fx_snd_smash = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS; // Per-pad smash send amount (0–1) — parallel-comp bus
fx_cmp_amt  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Per-pad compressor amount/mix (0=off, 1=full)
fx_cmp_mode = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Comp mode: 0=PUNCH 1=GLUE 2=SQUASH
fx_reso     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Per-pad filter resonance Q (0.707–12)

// Per-pad FX filter state (stereo — used by gap-flush)
fx_hpf_stL  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // HPF LP-state left
fx_hpf_stR  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // HPF LP-state right
fx_lpf_stL  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // LPF state left
fx_lpf_stR  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // LPF state right
// Residual energy left in this pad's chain, refreshed inside the processing
// branch from stages the sleep gate cannot see cheaply (right channel, EQ).
// One compare in the gate instead of six abs() per pad per sample.
fx_res      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // max |state| across the pad's recursive stages
// One-pole DC blocker state, TUBE only. Its curve is asymmetric BY DESIGN and
// the DC that produces has nowhere to go: the chain is HPF -> ... -> Drive, so
// the HPF its comment pointed at is five stages UPSTREAM.
fx_dc_x1L   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
fx_dc_y1L   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
fx_dc_x1R   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
fx_dc_y1R   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
// Per-pad control smoothers. The MASTER saturator drive has had one since it
// shipped (_sat_drv_sm); pan and the per-pad drive were written straight from
// the UI drag handlers into coefficients @sample multiplies, which is a step,
// which is a click.
p_panL_sm   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
p_panR_sm   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
fx_sat_drv_sm = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
fx_bc_cnt    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS; // Bitcrush hold counter
fx_bc_holdL  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS; // Bitcrush held sample L
fx_bc_holdR  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS; // Bitcrush held sample R
fx_bc_lvl    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS; // Precomputed quantization levels

// Per-pad compressor runtime state
fx_cmp_env      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Envelope follower state
fx_cmp_last_gr  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Cached GR (dB)
fx_cmp_last_lin = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Cached linear gain

// Per-pad compressor precomputed coefficients (set in recalc_fx → recalc_pad_comp)
fx_cmp_at_c       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Attack envelope coeff
fx_cmp_rel_c      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Release envelope coeff
fx_cmp_inv_ratio  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 1/ratio
fx_cmp_thresh     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Threshold dB
fx_cmp_knee_lo    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Knee lower bound dB
fx_cmp_knee_hi    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Knee upper bound dB
fx_cmp_knee_inv   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // 1/(2*knee)
fx_cmp_knee_lo_lin = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS; // Linear fast-path threshold
fx_cmp_makeup_lin = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Auto-makeup gain (linear)

// Per-pad SVF filters (rk_svf): HPF + LPF + low shelf + mid peak + high shelf = 5 per pad
// (RBJ biquads replaced by the Simper SVF 2026-06-10 — identical magnitude
// at the same knob values, verified in dev_tests/svf_parity_check.py, plus
// zipper-free coefficient glide (SVF_SMOOTH_MS one-pole chase; see
// rk_svf.jsfx-inc for the value). Master bus still uses rk_biquad.)
SVF_PER_PAD  = 6;
svf_pad      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * SVF_PER_PAD * SVF_STEREO_SIZE;
// Filter-slot offsets within per-pad SVF block
SVF_PAD_HPF  = 0;
SVF_PAD_LPF  = 1;
SVF_PAD_LO   = 2;
SVF_PAD_MID  = 3;
SVF_PAD_HI   = 4;
SVF_PAD_MID2 = 5;   // v46: 4th EQ band (second bell, "hi-mid")
// @init re-runs on srate change without clearing memory: reset every pad
// filter to unity/resting here; the recalc_fx + svf_snap pass below (and
// the @serialize restore path) re-establish the real curves.
i = 0; loop(NUM_SLOTS * SVF_PER_PAD,
  svf_init(svf_pad + i * SVF_STEREO_SIZE);
  i += 1;
);

// Master SVF filters: HPF + LPF + low shelf + mid peak + high shelf = 5
// (migrated from rk_biquad to rk_svf 2026-06-17 so the master EQ inherits the
// same one-pole zipper-free coefficient glide as the per-pad chain — the old
// biquads snapped coefficients per @block, audibly zippering on knob drags.
// Magnitude is identical at matching knob values per svf_parity_check.py.)
SVF_MST_COUNT = 5;
svf_master   = freemem; freemem += SVF_MST_COUNT * SVF_STEREO_SIZE;
SVF_MST_HPF  = 0;
SVF_MST_LPF  = 1;
SVF_MST_LO   = 2;
SVF_MST_MID  = 3;
SVF_MST_HI   = 4;
// @init re-runs on srate change without clearing memory: reset to unity/resting
// here; the recalc_global_fx + svf_snap pass below re-establishes real curves.
i = 0; loop(SVF_MST_COUNT,
  svf_init(svf_master + i * SVF_STEREO_SIZE);
  i += 1;
);

// Per-pad stereo accumulators (summed each sample, cleared each sample)
pad_accL    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
pad_accR    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
pad_awake   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;   // step 2b: 1 while the pad may be sounding (voices, Stretch ring, FX tail); pad_hi = highest awake + 1
pad_list    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;   // the awake pads, ascending, built at the end of each @block; pad_n of them (@sample visits only these)
pad_n = 0;

// FX knob memory: 12 knobs per pad (HPF/LPF/EQ_LO/EQ_MID/EQ_HI/SAT/BC_RATE/BC_BITS/DLY_SND/RVB_SND/CMP)
KM_FX_PER_PAD = 12;
km_fx       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * KM_FX_PER_PAD * KS;
KM_SYN_PER_PAD = 12;   // 8 macros + LEVEL + V.LO + V.HI (+1 spare)
km_syn      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * KM_SYN_PER_PAD * KS;

// ─── Global FX knob memory (3 knobs: HPF, LPF, SAT) ────────────────────
km_gfx_hpf  = freemem; freemem += KS;
km_gfx_lpf  = freemem; freemem += KS;
km_gfx_sat  = freemem; freemem += KS;

// ─── Global delay/reverb knob memory ────────────────────────────────────
// Delay: 4 knobs (DIV, FB, HPF, LPF)  Reverb: 3 knobs (SIZE, DAMP, WIDTH)
km_dly      = freemem; freemem += 4 * KS;
km_rvb      = freemem; freemem += 3 * KS;

// ─── Master EQ + Limiter knob memory ──────────────────────────────────
km_eq_lo    = freemem; freemem += KS;
km_eq_mid   = freemem; freemem += KS;
km_eq_hi    = freemem; freemem += KS;
km_lim_thr  = freemem; freemem += KS;
km_lim_rel  = freemem; freemem += KS;

// ─── Master VOL knob memory ──────────────────────────────────────────
km_master_vol = freemem; freemem += KS;

// ─── Console big-view knob memory (16 strips × PAN/DLY/RVB/SMS) ─────────
// rk_swing_ui_panels_mixer.jsfx-inc — the full-size console draws real
// rotary knobs for the four send rows; each needs a KS-slot hover/drag block.
// 4 was PAN + the three sends. 11 adds the SWING band's seven knobs -- HPF,
// LPF, RESO, RATE, BITS, DRIVE, COMP. ⚠️ Each knob needs its OWN slot: the lib
// keeps drag state in the slot, so two knobs sharing one would grab together.
KM_CON_PER_PAD = 11;
km_console  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * KM_CON_PER_PAD * KS;
km_comp     = freemem; freemem += 12 * KS;   // master COMP card: 6 knobs x 2 surfaces (big view, LCD)
// Master EQ page curve cache (Phase 4, D O-2): MEQ_CV_N sweep magnitudes, 3 node
// magnitudes, 3 node log-frequencies; keyed on the sixteen values in
// swing_panels_draw_eq. @gfx only.
// [0..79] the first 80 of the combined curve -- see MEQ_CV_SUM, [80..85] node
// magnitudes and log-frequencies, [86..87] spare, then MEQ_CV_SUM: the combined
// curve, MEQ_CV_N cells, then MEQ_CV_BANDS: each band's own curve, 5 rows x
// MEQ_CV_N (HPF, LPF, LO, MID, HI), for the per-band fills.
// ⭐ 512 points, not 80 (2026-09-21): at 80 a Q 4 bell was two or three points
// wide, its peak fell between them, and the curve drew as a clipped triangle
// beside ReEQ's smooth bell (the user put the two side by side). The cells sit
// below s_audio_start, so they move the pad region and everything above it up
// by ~3.2k cells (25 KB) against the HEADROOM BUDGET (~5M since 2026-09-23) -- noted, not
// ignored, and far below anything that budget has had to absorb.
MEQ_CV_N     = 512;
MEQ_CV_SUM   = 88;
MEQ_CV_BANDS = MEQ_CV_SUM + MEQ_CV_N;
meq_cv      = freemem; freemem += MEQ_CV_BANDS + 5 * MEQ_CV_N;
meq_cv_valid = 0;

// ─── Send bus accumulators (cleared each sample) ────────────────────────
snd_dly_accL = freemem; freemem += 1;
snd_dly_accR = freemem; freemem += 1;
snd_rvb_accL = freemem; freemem += 1;
snd_rvb_accR = freemem; freemem += 1;
snd_sms_accL = freemem; freemem += 1;
snd_sms_accR = freemem; freemem += 1;

// GUI state arrays (must be before audio buffers to avoid overlap)
pad_flash   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
patch_retL  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Patchbay loopback return, this sample (L), by ring pair column (read by nothing)
patch_retR  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Patchbay loopback return, this sample (R), by ring pair column
strip_tk    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad takeover: 1 = this pad's FX/gain/pan run on its Drum Strip
pad_bus     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // the channel each awake pad writes in @sample (set at the end of @block)
pad_wmode   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // Wired, per block (Outputs step 5): 1 = leaves pre-pan (the channel tap, a pair with one owner: the drain pans it back), 2 = a bank pair (leaves post-pan; its sends ride 34..37 to the ring beside it), 0 = post-pan (the bus tap, or not Wired)
patch_own   = freemem; freemem += PATCH_PCOLS;   // Wired, built at the end of each @block: the slot whose pan and sends the drain applies to each ring pair column -- bank A's sixteen = the slot in that position, a split pair = its owner, the send columns and the bank pairs = -1
patch_own_prev = freemem; freemem += PATCH_PCOLS; // the map the audio being drained LEFT under (the previous block's): what the drain reads
out_use_tmp = freemem; freemem += 64;         // the strip publish's pair counts + split owners (@block scratch, Outputs step 2)
strip_spl_own  = freemem; freemem += OUT_PAIRS - OUT_PAIR_SPLIT;  // banks B..D's Drum Strips: split pair k's owner (slot, -1 none), set by each strip publish
strip_spl_want = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;                   // @block scratch: 1 = this slot hands over to its split pair's strip
memset(strip_spl_own, -1, OUT_PAIRS - OUT_PAIR_SPLIT);
// The bank colour sets (2026-10-15; the user: "can i give the users options" -- the THEME menu's BANK COLOURS row,
// slider47 bank_col_set). Set s (1..5), bank b (0..3), channel c: bank_set_rgb[(s - 1) * 12 + b * 3 + c], 0..255.
// Read by the bank tabs (@gfx, swing_grid_bank_rgb) and the strip publish (@block, for the bridge's bank tracks);
// written here only. Set 0 = Off: plain tabs (the look before colours), and the bridge paints no bank track.
BANK_COL_SETS = 5;
bank_set_rgb = freemem; freemem += BANK_COL_SETS * 12;
_bs_i = 0;
loop(BANK_COL_SETS * 12,
  bank_set_rgb[_bs_i] =
    // 1 Classic: blue, amber, green, violet (the first colours, 2026-10-15)
    _bs_i ==  0 ?  70 : _bs_i ==  1 ? 130 : _bs_i ==  2 ? 200 :  _bs_i ==  3 ? 205 : _bs_i ==  4 ? 135 : _bs_i ==  5 ?  45 :
    _bs_i ==  6 ?  85 : _bs_i ==  7 ? 165 : _bs_i ==  8 ?  95 :  _bs_i ==  9 ? 165 : _bs_i == 10 ?  95 : _bs_i == 11 ? 190 :
    // 2 Hardware: red, yellow, green, blue
    _bs_i == 12 ? 205 : _bs_i == 13 ?  70 : _bs_i == 14 ?  70 :  _bs_i == 15 ? 220 : _bs_i == 16 ? 180 : _bs_i == 17 ?  50 :
    _bs_i == 18 ?  80 : _bs_i == 19 ? 170 : _bs_i == 20 ?  90 :  _bs_i == 21 ?  70 : _bs_i == 22 ? 130 : _bs_i == 23 ? 210 :
    // 3 Warm to cool: coral, gold, teal, indigo
    _bs_i == 24 ? 220 : _bs_i == 25 ? 110 : _bs_i == 26 ?  80 :  _bs_i == 27 ? 215 : _bs_i == 28 ? 170 : _bs_i == 29 ?  60 :
    _bs_i == 30 ?  60 : _bs_i == 31 ? 165 : _bs_i == 32 ? 150 :  _bs_i == 33 ?  95 : _bs_i == 34 ? 100 : _bs_i == 35 ? 200 :
    // 4 Studio muted: slate, sand, sage, mauve
    _bs_i == 36 ?  95 : _bs_i == 37 ? 120 : _bs_i == 38 ? 150 :  _bs_i == 39 ? 170 : _bs_i == 40 ? 145 : _bs_i == 41 ? 105 :
    _bs_i == 42 ? 115 : _bs_i == 43 ? 145 : _bs_i == 44 ? 115 :  _bs_i == 45 ? 145 : _bs_i == 46 ? 110 : _bs_i == 47 ? 145 :
    // 5 Neon: cyan, magenta, lime, orange
    _bs_i == 48 ?  40 : _bs_i == 49 ? 200 : _bs_i == 50 ? 230 :  _bs_i == 51 ? 220 : _bs_i == 52 ?  70 : _bs_i == 53 ? 180 :
    _bs_i == 54 ? 150 : _bs_i == 55 ? 210 : _bs_i == 56 ?  60 :  _bs_i == 57 ? 250 : _bs_i == 58 ? 140 : 40;
  _bs_i += 1;
);
out_menu_val = freemem; freemem += 32;        // the Out menu's result -> value (@gfx; swing_out_menu, Outputs step 3)
pad_meterL  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad peak level meters (L)
pad_meterR  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // per-pad peak level meters (R)
pc          = freemem; freemem += NUM_PADS;

// ─── Preserve-on-reload snapshot shadows ───────────────────────────────────
// Audio-only reloads (GS_KIT_PRESERVE_LIVE == 1: project-open sidecar load
// or Undo/chunk-restore audio-repair) snapshot the @serialize-restored live
// per-pad params here on kit-import entry, then restore them after the audio
// copy — so the kit file's stored values can't clobber the user's session.
// Only the fields the kit-import META read overwrites are shadowed; pure
// audio-structural fields (s_len, s_sr, p_layer_cnt, l_len, l_sr) are left
// to load fresh from the kit (a restored length could index past the loaded
// buffer). Globals are preserved by gating the kit-import globals block.
// (See swing_kit_preserve_snapshot / _restore in rk_swing_ui_state.jsfx-inc.)
// Pad NAME strings, as char codes rather than string slots. memcpy cannot
// shadow a string, which is why names were left out of the preserve snapshot
// to begin with -- so this borrows the undo engine's proven shape
// (udo_s2_name): 33 cells of cname then 33 of name, per pad -- 33, because
// PNE_MAX_LEN is 32 and a full 32-char name still needs its terminator.
sv_pad_names     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * 66;
sv_p_gain        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_pan         = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_tune        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_attack      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_decay       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_sustain     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_release     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_adsr_user   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_mute        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_solo        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_output      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
// p_note / p_note_lock intentionally NOT preserved (kit-layout routing, not a
// session tuning) — see swing_kit_preserve_snapshot in rk_swing_ui_state.jsfx-inc.
sv_p_color       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_choke       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_oneshot     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_reverse     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_hpf_freq   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_lpf_freq   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_lo      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_mid     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_mid2    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_mid_q   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_mid2_q  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_lo_q    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_hi_q    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_hi      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_sat_drv    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_drv_mode   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_bc_rate    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_bc_bits    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_snd_dly    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_snd_rvb    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_snd_smash  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_lo_freq = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_mid_freq= freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_mid2_freq= freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_fx_eq_hi_freq = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_sum_tight   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_rpt_div     = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_layer_mode  = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_s_start       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_s_end         = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_s_norm        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_s_norm_gain   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_sample_offset = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_p_rng_lo        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // preserve-live shadow of chromatic range (semis below root)
sv_p_rng_hi        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;  // preserve-live shadow of chromatic range (semis above root)
sv_l_start       = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;
sv_l_end         = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;
sv_l_norm        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;
sv_l_norm_gain   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;
sv_l_vel_lo      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;
sv_l_vel_hi      = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;
sv_l_rr_order    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;
sv_l_gain        = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS * MAX_LAYERS;
// preserve-live shadows for the SYN slot (chunk state wins over kit file)
sv_ps_enable   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_engine   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_level    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_vel_lo   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_vel_hi   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_rr_order = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_mac0 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_mac1 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_mac2 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_mac3 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_mac4 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_mac5 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_mac6 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
sv_ps_mac7 = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;

// LCD bar (knob memory)
freemem = swing_lcd_init(freemem);

// KIT-tab note/change map (16 per-pad outcome codes)
freemem = swing_chgmap_init(freemem);
freemem = swing_kitcover_init(freemem);
// Pad→category post queue: the synth autonamer (icon parity) and native sample
// DROPS both queue here, and the main @gfx drains ONE post per 4th frame through
// the single-slot PADCAT mailbox (batch posts would drop all but the last;
// bridge polls per defer tick). -100 = nothing pending; else the cat request to
// post (glyph id, -1 = Auto re-infer, EON_PADCAT_NONE = the user cleared it).
_syn_cat_pend = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
memset(_syn_cat_pend, -100, NUM_SLOTS);
// Parallel SRC hint for each queued post. -1 = leave the pad's provenance
// alone (the synth path wants this); 2 = the user's own sample, which is what a
// native drop means and what makes FILL leave the pad alone afterwards.
// ⚠️ Must exist: an unallocated array base reads 0 in EEL2, so `_syn_cat_src[p]`
// would write over memory[0..15] — the head of the very first freemem block.
_syn_cat_src = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;
memset(_syn_cat_src, -1, NUM_SLOTS);
// (This block used to sit ~500 lines below, with the other gmem bands. It
//  had to move UP here: swing_fxview_init sizes its buffer as
//  FXP_REC_MAX * FXP_REC, and an EEL2 name that has not been assigned yet
//  reads 0 -- so the picker reserved ZERO cells, freemem did not advance,
//  and swing_color_init below was handed the very same address. The
//  published plugin list then landed on top of col_rgba, which is why
//  opening the picker recoloured every pad in the instrument. A constant
//  must be defined ABOVE any allocation that sizes itself from it;
//  nothing warns, the arithmetic just quietly comes out 0.)
// ── EON_FXPICK: the FX picker's JSFX <-> Lua exchange ──────────────────────
// Declared in .refs/gmem_regions_supplement.tsv BEFORE any gmem[] touched it;
// the audit fails on undeclared access. 26345472 = 402 * 65536, block-aligned.
//
// TWO INDEPENDENT SEQUENCES, and the split is the whole design:
//   REQ_SEQ carries VIEW STATE (scroll, query, filters). Coalescing is CORRECT
//     here -- dropping intermediate scroll positions is what makes a live-typed
//     search box affordable.
//   ACT_SEQ carries MUTATIONS (swap, insert, delete). These must never be
//     dropped, so the face posts one and waits for ACT_ACK before the next.
// One mailbox for both would lose a swap the moment a fast scroll coalesced
// past it.
//
// Every write is PAYLOAD FIRST, SEQ LAST -- the reader is edge-triggered on the
// seq, so the data has to be in place before the seq announces it. Response
// seq is a seqlock: odd = mid-write, even = stable.
EON_FXPICK_BASE   = 26345472;
EON_FXPICK_STRIDE = 4096;
EON_FXPICK_SLOTS  = 16;          // matches the instance registry cap
EON_FXPICK_TBL    = 26411008;    // 403 * 65536 -- flat shared string tables
EON_FXPICK_TBL_N  = 8192;

// ── EON_CONSOLE_INS: what is in each PAD's own track chain ───────────────
// The picker band above publishes ONE chain for ONE target. A console strip
// wants sixteen at once and only a SUMMARY of each -- enough to draw a lit
// slot in its category colour. Names stay in the hover popover; they were
// never going to fit on a 44 px strip.
//
// Declared in .refs/gmem_regions_supplement.tsv before this line existed.
// 26476544 = 404 * 65536, block-aligned and prefaulted below.
//
// ⚠️ A slot word packs three things and is decoded by ARITHMETIC, never by
// shifts: EEL2 << is 32-bit with the count masked mod 32, and the offline
// bit sits high enough to make that a real hazard rather than a theoretical
// one (.docs/wiki/01, the StepSeq 49-lane near-miss).
//     -1        = slot empty
//     cat       = 0..31  category index, drives the colour
//     +64       = bypassed
//     +128      = offline
EON_CONINS_BASE   = 26542080;   // 405 * 65536
EON_CONINS_STRIDE = 2048;
EON_CONINS_SLOTS  = 16;
CI_SEQ    = 0;    // seqlock, even = stable, written LAST
CI_HB     = 1;    // COUNTER, not a clock: the face has no wall clock to
                  // compare against and only needs to know it moved
CI_FLAGS  = 2;    // bit0: multi-out tracks · bit1: could not look them up
// ⭐ LAYOUT VERSION. The bridge is a running script: every record change I make
// only takes effect when it is restarted, and until then it keeps writing the
// OLD shape into the new one. That has now silently produced two mysteries --
// blank cards once, garbled names once -- where the face was faithfully
// drawing whatever the stale bridge left. Bump this whenever the record moves,
// and the face SAYS SO instead of rendering the wreckage.
CI_FMT    = 3;    // published layout version
CI_FMT_VER = 3;   // what THIS face understands (3: the records are the strips of the bank in CI_BANK, step 5)
// The bank on screen the sixteen strip records were built for (0..3). Record i is strip i of THAT bank: its
// slot's track in multi-out (a bank A pad's, a bank's or a split pad's), its slot's Wired container in stereo.
// The face draws them only while it shows the same bank (a bank switch waits one publish).
CI_BANK   = 4;
CI_HDR    = 32;   // first record
CI_PREC   = 118;  // words per record
CI_NSLOT  = 8;    // slots per record
CI_COUNT  = 0;    // -1 = owns no REAPER track
CI_SLOT   = 1;    // +1..+8  category + bypass/offline, one word each
CI_NAME   = 9;    // +9..+104 eight names, CI_NAMEW words each
CI_NAMEW  = 12;   // per name: length, then CI_NCHAR characters
CI_NCHAR  = 11;   // ⚠️ TRUNCATED, and DISPLAY ONLY -- the tooltip, nothing else.
// ⭐ THE CARD COMES FROM A HASH THE BRIDGE COMPUTES OVER THE FULL NAME, not
// from the truncated one above. Hashing 11 characters of "EON Drum Strip"
// finds nothing: the deck is keyed on the whole name, so a truncated hash
// silently misses every plugin whose name is longer than the field -- which
// is most of them, and was about to make the Drum Strip card I just drew
// invisible. One published word beats widening every name field instead.
CI_HASH   = 105;  // +105..+112, one card-name hash per slot
CI_RECS   = 17;   // 16 strips (the bank in CI_BANK), then the MASTER as record 16
// Face-side only, past everything the bridge publishes: the resolved card per
// slot, looked up once per publish rather than per frame.
CI_CARD   = CI_HASH + CI_NSLOT;              // 105 + 8 = 113
CI_VIS    = CI_CARD + CI_NSLOT;              // 113 + 8 = 121: face-side, visible ROW -> real slot (-1 = none)
CI_VISN   = CI_VIS + CI_NSLOT;               // 129: rows visible (house plugins may be hidden)
CIF_REC   = CI_VISN + 1;                     // 130 words per face record

// response half (bridge writes, face reads)
FXP_PUB_SEQ  = 0;    // seqlock, even = stable, written LAST
FXP_GEN      = 1;    // bumped per publish; the face re-snapshots on change
FXP_ANS_REQ  = 2;    // echo of the REQ_SEQ this page answers
FXP_TOTAL    = 5;    // rows matching the current query
FXP_WIN_OFF  = 6;
FXP_WIN_N    = 7;
FXP_FLAGS    = 15;   // bit0 frozen, bit1 no EnumInstalledFX, bit2 no target
FXP_HB       = 16;   // bridge liveness, os.time()
FXP_FMT_VER  = 17;

// request half (face writes, bridge reads)
FXP_REQ_SEQ  = 64;
FXP_REQ_OFF  = 69;
FXP_REQ_N    = 70;

// row block: 48 records of 64 cells at +192
// ⚠️⚠️ THE BLOCK MUST LAND EXACTLY ON FXP_CHAIN (3264) AND IT STILL DOES:
// 192 + 48*64 = 3264, where it used to be 192 + 64*48. Vendor needed 16 more
// words per row and the record was FULL, so the width was bought back out of
// the row COUNT rather than by growing the band -- growing it would have
// pushed the chain area over a stride boundary and moved a second thing.
// 48 rows is still far more than any page asks for: the list shows ~20 and
// asks for double that.
FXP_ROWS     = 192;
FXP_REC      = 64;
FXP_REC_MAX  = 48;
FXP_R_LEN    = 0;    // name length; 0 = empty row
FXP_R_NAME   = 1;    // 40 chars, one per cell
FXP_R_FMT    = 42;   // format code
FXP_R_BUCKET = 43;   // bucket index into M.BUCKETS
FXP_R_KIND   = 44;
FXP_R_RIDX   = 45;   // index into the engine's unfiltered enumeration = the pick handle
FXP_R_CARD   = 46;
// Word 47, CHAINS mode only: a preview of what is INSIDE a chain file.
// ⚠️ ONE word, because the row record is full -- 192 + 64*48 lands exactly on
// the chain area at 3264, so the record cannot grow without moving that too.
// Four category indices and a count, packed by MULTIPLICATION and unpacked by
// division: EEL2 shifts are 32-bit with the count masked mod 32, and this
// value reaches ~32.5M. gmem cells are doubles, so the precision is there.
//   w = c1 + 32*c2 + 1024*c3 + 32768*c4 + 1048576*n
FXP_R_CHSTK  = 47;
// Vendor, words 48..63: length then 15 chars. The registry has PARSED it since
// P1 (rk_lua_fxpicker's parse_name returns name, vendor, fmt, path) and threw
// it away at the wire -- nothing new is being worked out, only carried.
// 15 chars covers what matters: Cockos, Waves, u-he, Tokyo Dawn, Valhalla.
FXP_R_VLEN   = 48;
FXP_R_VEND   = 49;   // 15 chars, 49..63
FXP_VEND_MAX = 15;
// ── chain half (bridge writes, face reads) ──
// Its OWN seqlock: the chain moves when the user touches another track
// or edits FX in REAPER's window, which never bumps REQ_SEQ. Sharing the
// row page's PUB_SEQ would re-snapshot 3072 row cells on every chain poll.
FXP_CH_SEQ   = 3;    // seqlock, even = stable, written LAST
FXP_CH_N     = 18;   // slots on the target track
FXP_CH_SEL   = 19;   // focused slot, -1 = none
FXP_TGT_LEN  = 20;   // target track name length
FXP_TGT_NAME = 21;   // 32 chars, 21..52
// REAPER's own track number (IP_TRACKNUMBER, 1-based; 0 = no target). The
// bridge already read this to build the "Track 12" FALLBACK name, but threw it
// away whenever the track HAD a name -- so the one thing that tells two
// identically-named tracks apart was never published. Word 53: the first free
// cell above the name it belongs to (54..63 remain free; Q starts at 77).
FXP_TGT_NUM  = 53;
// The target track's own colour, packed r*65536 + g*256 + b; -1 = the track has
// no custom colour and REAPER is drawing it in the theme default.
// ⚠️ The track ICON is deliberately NOT here. P_ICON is an absolute PATH, up to
// 255 characters, and this band has 8 free words before the query starts -- a
// path needs its own channel, plus an image slot and a load that never runs per
// frame. The colour is one word and carries most of the same "which track am I
// on" answer, so it lands first and the icon stays a separate job.
FXP_TGT_COL  = 56;
// Face→bridge: 1 = HOLD this target, stop following REAPER's last-touched
// track. Word 54 (55..63 still free). Written every frame the FX page draws,
// so the face and the bridge cannot disagree after a restart of either.
FXP_TGT_PIN  = 54;
// Face→bridge kind filter, word 55: 0 = FX only (everything that is NOT an
// instrument) · 1 = instruments only · 2 = both. ⭐ The registry ALREADY knows
// which is which -- rk_lua_fx_recipes tags every row fx/instrument/midi/other
// and the bridge publishes it as FXP_R_KIND -- the picker simply never offered
// the filter. 2 is the default because it is what the list has always shown.
FXP_KINDF    = 55;
// Face→bridge, word 57, written with an aim (before TGT_SEQ): what FXP_TGT_PAD names. 0 = a console strip, i.e.
// one of bank A's sixteen output tracks (pair 0..15; -1 the master) -- what every older Swing means; 1 = a SLOT
// (0..63, the FX tab following the selected pad): the bridge aims at the track that slot plays through now, its
// bank's track or its own for a bank B-D pad (Pad Banks Outputs step 3; the slot's pair is the strip band's OUT_PAIR).
FXP_TGT_KIND = 57;
// 32 records of 24 at +3264 -- exactly where the row block ends
// (192 + 48*64 = 3264), running to 4032 inside the 4096 stride.
FXP_CHAIN     = 3264;
// ⚠️ 25, not 24. FXP_C_OFF (offline, published) and FXP_C_CARD (the face's
// locally-resolved card) BOTH landed on word 23: the snapshot copies gmem
// in, then the face writes the card over the top, and offline silently read
// as always-false. Two owners, one word, no warning. The chain area is
// 32*25 = 800 at offset 3264, ending 4063 -- still inside the 4096 stride.
FXP_CREC      = 25;
FXP_CHAIN_MAX = 32;
FXP_C_LEN    = 0;    // name length; 0 = empty slot
FXP_C_NAME   = 1;    // 20 chars
FXP_C_ON     = 21;   // 1 = enabled, 0 = bypassed
FXP_C_FMT    = 22;
FXP_C_OFF    = 23;   // 1 = OFFLINE. Distinct from bypassed: bypassed still
                     // loads and passes audio, offline is unloaded entirely.
FXP_C_CARD   = 24;   // FACE-LOCAL resolved card, as FXP_R_CARD. Must stay
                     // ABOVE every published word -- it is written over the
                     // snapshot after the copy.

// ── action mailbox ──
// SEPARATE from REQ_SEQ and deliberately NOT coalescing. REQ_SEQ drops
// intermediate values, which is right for a scroll position and fatal
// for a swap. The face posts one action and waits for ACT_ACK.
FXP_ACT_ACK  = 4;    // response half: bridge echoes the seq it ran
FXP_ACT_SEQ  = 72;   // request half, written LAST
FXP_ACT_VERB = 73;
FXP_ACT_A    = 74;   // chain slot, or -1
FXP_ACT_B    = 75;   // registry row index (FXP_R_RIDX)
FXA_SWAP     = 1;    // replace slot A with registry row B
FXA_INSERT   = 2;    // insert row B after slot A (-1 = append)
FXA_ENABLE   = 3;    // toggle bypass on slot A
FXA_REMOVE   = 4;    // delete slot A
// Console strip menu verbs. EMBED is an ACTION, never a toggle: REAPER
// exposes no way to read back whether an FX is embedded, so the face cannot
// know which way a toggle should go. OFFLINE is a real toggle -- the bridge
// reads that one back.
FXA_EMBED_TCP = 6;   // show slot A embedded in the track control panel
FXA_EMBED_MCP = 7;   // ...or the mixer control panel
FXA_OFFLINE   = 8;   // toggle offline on slot A
FXA_MOVE     = 5;    // move slot A to index B
// query, request half. 63 chars at +77 -- ends at 139, well clear of
// the row block at 192.
FXP_Q_LEN    = 76;
FXP_Q        = 77;
FXP_Q_MAX    = 63;
FXP_BANK     = 141;  // selected rail row, -1 = ALL

// ── Console -> picker targeting (request half, +142..144) ────────────────
// Clicking an insert slot on a console strip has to say WHICH chain the
// picker should now be looking at. Until this existed the bridge used
// GetLastTouchedTrack(), which is right for "open the picker on whatever I
// just clicked in REAPER" and useless for "this pad, that slot".
//
// Seq-gated like every other request: payload first, seq LAST. Coalescing is
// CORRECT here -- if two clicks land in one bridge tick, the second one is
// the one you meant.
FXP_TGT_SEQ  = 142;  // bumped by the face, written LAST
FXP_TGT_PAD  = 143;  // 0..15 = that pad's track · -1 = the master/bus track
FXP_TGT_SLOT = 144;  // chain slot to focus, -1 = none

// ── CHAINS mode (request half, +145..186) ────────────────────────────────
// ⭐ Chains ride the SAME rows channel as plugins. A chain file is just a row
// that happens to be a file, so paging, scrolling, the publish path and the
// row renderer all work unchanged -- a parallel channel would have been a
// second copy of every one of those.
//
// The rail becomes the FXChains/ folder tree. ONE level at a time plus a
// breadcrumb, not a recursive walk with expand triangles (spec §2), which is
// also why the request carries a relative path rather than a tree state.
FXP_CHMODE   = 145;  // 0 = plugin registry · 1 = FXChains listing
FXP_CHREL_LEN = 146; // length of the relative folder path, 0 = root
FXP_CHREL    = 147;  // +147..186, 40 chars
FXP_CHREL_MAX = 40;
// Row kinds the bridge sends back in CHAINS mode. 0..3 are plugin kinds
// (fx / instrument / midi / other), so these continue the same space rather
// than overloading one of them.
FXK_CHAIN    = 4;    // a .RfxChain file
FXK_FOLDER   = 5;    // a subfolder — clicking it navigates
// Chain actions.
FXA_CHAIN_APPLY = 9; // replace the target chain with row B
FXA_CHAIN_SAVE  = 10;// save the target chain as a new .RfxChain
// ⭐ FLOAT is what a click on a plugin is EXPECTED to do. Opening the picker
// is the SWAP affordance -- useful, but not what "click the thing" means in
// any DAW. TrackFX_Show(tr, fx, 3) floats the plugin's own window.
FXA_FLOAT       = 11;// float slot A's own plugin window

// ── bank table, in the SHARED table block ──
// Registry-global: the same list for every Swing, so it does not belong
// in a per-instance band. Its own seqlock -- banks change when the user
// edits REAPER's FX folders, which no other sequence knows about.
FXP_TB_N     = 0;
FXP_TB_SEQ   = 1;    // even = stable, written LAST
FXP_TB       = 16;
FXP_TREC     = 40;
FXP_TB_MAX   = 48;
FXP_TB_LEN   = 0;
FXP_TB_NAME  = 1;    // 24 chars
FXP_TB_KIND  = 25;   // 0 all, 1 recent, 2 folder, 3 category
FXP_TB_BUCK  = 26;   // bucket index for kind 3, else -1
FXP_TB_COUNT = 27;
   // FACE-LOCAL: resolved card record, or -1. Not part of
                     // the wire protocol -- the bridge never writes it; the
                     // face fills it once per published page so the name
                     // hash is not recomputed every frame for every row.

// ⚠️ PREFAULT — force NSEEL to allocate both blocks.
// REAPER allocates named-gmem in lazy 65536-slot blocks, and .docs/wiki/
// 05-memory-and-gmem.md says only a JSFX write triggers it. Whether
// reaper.gmem_write does is UNTESTED, and every existing bridge-published band
// happens to share its block with a cell the JSFX also writes -- so none of
// them proves the Lua-only case. If Lua writes do NOT allocate, the picker's
// whole publish drops on the floor and the list is silently, permanently
// empty. Two writes make the question moot. Same fix as the stretch rings
// (rk_swing_block_pitch.jsfx-inc:183).
gmem[EON_FXPICK_BASE + EON_FXPICK_STRIDE * EON_FXPICK_SLOTS - 1] = 0;  // block 402
gmem[EON_FXPICK_TBL + EON_FXPICK_TBL_N - 1] = 0;                       // block 403
gmem[EON_CONINS_BASE + EON_CONINS_STRIDE * EON_CONINS_SLOTS - 1] = 0;  // block 405

// Console insert snapshot: 16 pads x (count + 8 slot words). Copied out of
// gmem under the seqlock so the strip draws from a stable picture -- the
// bridge republishes on its own clock and a half-written chain would blink
// slots in and out mid-frame.
// ⚠️ Sized by CIF_REC, the record the reader actually writes. It was sized
// for an older layout (105 words) while the reader wrote 121 per record --
// 272 words of overrun into whatever freemem handed out next, on every
// console publish. Found 2026-09-07 while adding the visible-row map.
_conins_buf = freemem; freemem += CI_RECS * CIF_REC;
_conins_seq = -1;      // last seqlock value consumed
_conins_hb    = -1;    // last heartbeat COUNTER seen from the bridge
_conins_hb_t  = 0;     // time_precise() when it last moved
_conins_maxn  = 0;     // FX on the fullest channel -- drives how many slots
                       // every strip draws, and therefore how big a card gets
_conins_stale = 1;     // 1 = the bridge is not answering; start pessimistic,
                       // because "no data yet" and "no bridge" look the same
                       // and only one of them is safe to draw as fact.

freemem = swing_kitsview_init(freemem);   // kits-view roster snapshot buffers
freemem = swing_fxview_init(freemem);     // FX picker published-page buffer
freemem = swing_fb_init(freemem);         // mini browser published-page buffer
freemem = swing_fb_prv_init(freemem);     // browser preview voice (~11 s)
freemem = swing_fxcard_data_init(freemem); // 145 card recipes + name keys
freemem = swing_ldr_init(freemem);        // sliced loader: two job records (block bank + UI bank)

// Color system (pre-computed RGBA)
freemem = swing_color_init(freemem);

// Custom popup menu (rk_swing_popup.jsfx-inc) — Swing-styled replacement for
// gfx_showmenu. Used by MODE/ALGO stepper today; other right-click sites
// migrate incrementally as they're next touched.
freemem = swing_popup_init(freemem);

// Big View: MAPPING keyboard x-index buffer
freemem = swing_mapping_init(freemem);

// Selection state
sel_pad = 0;

// Anti-pop crossfade: stores last output per channel for smooth transitions
_xf_prev    = freemem; freemem += OUT_PAIRS * 2;  // previous output values, every pin (16 buses, the returns, the bank / split pairs)

// ─── Internal PARAM undo/redo engine state (v2, Phase 1A) ─────────────────
// Field tables = the single source of truth for which per-pad arrays the undo
// engine (rk_drumkit_dsp.jsfx-inc) snapshots: undoable scalars + per-layer
// metadata. NOT audio, NOT names/paths. Built HERE because every per-pad array
// it points at is already allocated above; consumed by the engine functions at
// run-time. Session-volatile (freemem) — undo history clears on reinstantiate.
UDO_NS     = 69;                              // scalar fields per pad (54 + 14 SYN slot + smash send)
UDO_NL     = 8;                               // per-layer fields per pad
UDO_STRIDE = UDO_NS + UDO_NL * MAX_LAYERS;    // packed floats per pad snapshot
UDO_DEPTH  = 32;                              // undo / redo ring depth
// udo_fs[10] = p_output: a pad's OUTPUT CHOICE stays out of the param undo (2026-10-16; the user: "the output returns
// to the bank but undo does not remove the track") -- REAPER's undo owns it, together with the track the bridge makes
// for it (strip OUT_UREQ). undo_unpack skips the field under _udo_skip_out (the param ring's undo / redo) and the
// commit's change test ignores it; the structural restore (a whole pad, a kit) still carries it.
UDO_K_OUT  = 10;

udo_fs = freemem; freemem += UDO_NS;          // scalar field base-pointer table
udo_fl = freemem; freemem += UDO_NL;          // per-layer field base-pointer table
udo_fs[0]=p_gain;        udo_fs[1]=p_pan;          udo_fs[2]=p_tune;          udo_fs[3]=p_attack;
udo_fs[4]=p_decay;       udo_fs[5]=p_sustain;      udo_fs[6]=p_release;       udo_fs[7]=p_adsr_user;
udo_fs[8]=p_mute;        udo_fs[9]=p_solo;         udo_fs[10]=p_output;       udo_fs[11]=p_note;
udo_fs[12]=p_note_lock;  udo_fs[13]=p_color;       udo_fs[14]=p_choke;        udo_fs[15]=p_oneshot;
udo_fs[16]=p_reverse;    udo_fs[17]=p_swapLR;      udo_fs[18]=p_sum_tight;    udo_fs[19]=p_rpt_div;
udo_fs[20]=p_layer_mode; udo_fs[21]=p_sample_offset; udo_fs[22]=s_start;      udo_fs[23]=s_end;
udo_fs[24]=s_norm;       udo_fs[25]=s_norm_gain;   udo_fs[26]=s_skip;         udo_fs[27]=fx_hpf_freq;
udo_fs[28]=fx_lpf_freq;  udo_fs[29]=fx_reso;       udo_fs[30]=fx_eq_lo;       udo_fs[31]=fx_eq_mid;
udo_fs[32]=fx_eq_mid2;   udo_fs[33]=fx_eq_hi;      udo_fs[34]=fx_eq_lo_freq;  udo_fs[35]=fx_eq_mid_freq;
udo_fs[36]=fx_eq_mid2_freq; udo_fs[37]=fx_eq_hi_freq; udo_fs[38]=fx_eq_lo_q;  udo_fs[39]=fx_eq_mid_q;
udo_fs[40]=fx_eq_mid2_q; udo_fs[41]=fx_eq_hi_q;    udo_fs[42]=fx_sat_drv;     udo_fs[43]=fx_drv_mode;
udo_fs[44]=fx_bc_rate;   udo_fs[45]=fx_bc_bits;    udo_fs[46]=fx_snd_dly;     udo_fs[47]=fx_snd_rvb;
udo_fs[68]=fx_snd_smash;
udo_fs[48]=fx_cmp_amt;   udo_fs[49]=fx_cmp_mode;   udo_fs[50]=sp_pitch_mode;  udo_fs[51]=sp_pitch_algo;
udo_fs[52]=p_rng_lo;     udo_fs[53]=p_rng_hi;
udo_fs[54]=ps_enable;    udo_fs[55]=ps_engine;     udo_fs[56]=ps_level;    udo_fs[57]=ps_vel_lo;
udo_fs[58]=ps_vel_hi;    udo_fs[59]=ps_rr_order;   udo_fs[60]=ps_mac0;     udo_fs[61]=ps_mac1;
udo_fs[62]=ps_mac2;      udo_fs[63]=ps_mac3;       udo_fs[64]=ps_mac4;     udo_fs[65]=ps_mac5;
udo_fs[66]=ps_mac6;      udo_fs[67]=ps_mac7;
udo_fl[0]=l_start;       udo_fl[1]=l_end;          udo_fl[2]=l_norm;          udo_fl[3]=l_norm_gain;
udo_fl[4]=l_vel_lo;      udo_fl[5]=l_vel_hi;       udo_fl[6]=l_rr_order;       udo_fl[7]=l_gain;

udo_base    = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS  * UDO_STRIDE;  // per-pad pre-edit baseline
udo_ust     = freemem; freemem += UDO_DEPTH * UDO_STRIDE;  // undo ring (packed entries)
udo_urd     = freemem; freemem += UDO_DEPTH * UDO_STRIDE;  // redo ring
udo_ust_pad = freemem; freemem += UDO_DEPTH;               // pad index per undo entry
udo_urd_pad = freemem; freemem += UDO_DEPTH;               // pad index per redo entry
_udo_pend   = freemem; freemem += NUM_SLOTS;                // per-pad "changed this gesture"
udo_cmp     = freemem; freemem += UDO_STRIDE;              // scratch: change-detect vs baseline in commit
_udo_uc = 0; _udo_rc = 0; _udo_applying = 0; _udo_skip_out = 0;

// ─── Phase 2: structural (audio) undo — COMMAND pattern, 1-level ──────────
// Instead of snapshotting the whole kit (memory-heavy, what the field avoids),
// each structural op records only what it needs to reverse:
//   per-pad (load/clear/clear-layer) → back up that ONE pad's slot + metadata
//   swap                              → self-inverse (just the two indices)
//   kit / new / clear-all            → deferred (sidecar reload); invalidates entry
// The one-pad audio backup buffer (udo_s2_audio) is allocated after the audio
// region (near _send_fx_mem). Scoped restore => no collateral on other pads.
udo_st_meta = freemem; freemem += UDO_STRIDE;             // ONE pad's param/layer pack (undo_pack)
udo_s2_aud  = freemem; freemem += 16;                     // one pad: s_len,s_sr,p_layer_cnt + l_len/l_sr/sp_baked_tune x4
udo_s2_name = freemem; freemem += 1432;                   // one pad: cname(33)+name(33)+path(272)+4 layer paths(4*272) char codes (P3: LPATH undo fix; 33 per name so a full 32-char name keeps its terminator)
_udo_st_valid = 0;       // 1 = a structural undo entry exists
udo_s2_type = 0;         // 1 = per-pad, 2 = swap, 3 = kit (deferred)
udo_s2_pad  = -1; udo_s2_pad2 = -1;
_udo_swap_req = 0;       // deferred swap-undo request (processed in @gfx)
_udo_nl_t = 0;           // wheel / right-button undo bracket: time of the last notch, 0 = none open (D-9)
_udo_rebase_req = 0;     // a finished load asks the @gfx head to re-base the undo snapshot (D-8; set from @block)
_udo_name_req = 0; _udo_name_pad = -1;  // deferred per-pad name-restore (processed in @gfx)

// ─── Kit-level undo (disk-based) ────────────────────────────────────────────
// Load Kit / New Kit / Clear All are undone by RELOADING a temp .swing the
// bridge silently dumps right before the op (CMD 83 dump → CMD 82 reload).
// No in-memory kit backup: a whole kit is up to 64M, and the 2026-06 attempt to keep
// one above the pool was measured past the grant (see the maxmem note at the
// options line, corrected 2026-09-23); it stays disk-based.
_udo_kitundo_req = 0;    // engine → @gfx: fire CMD 82 (reload the undo sidecar)
_udo_cap_depth = 0;      // re-entrancy depth (outermost op records the entry)
_udo_ready = 0;          // set after udo_s2_audio is allocated + fits __memtop()
udo_s2_extent = 0;       // cells the last one-pad capture has SAVED (undo_capture_pad)
// Sliced capture (2026-09-09): a full-extent memcpy is up to 32 MB on the audio
// thread at the head of a drop -- the last big one left after the EON_PADPCM
// stream moved the file read off it (10 ms for a 40 s pad, measured 2026-09-08).
// A caller that promises to pump udo_cow_upto before every write into the slot
// sets _udo_cap_lazy_req; the capture then copies NOTHING up front and saves each
// region a bounded slice at a time, just before a writer destroys it. That makes
// udo_s2_extent "cells actually saved", and it grows -- the restore copies exactly
// that prefix, because everything above it was never written and so still holds
// the original audio.
_udo_cap_lazy_req = 0;   // set around ONE undo_begin_pad call by a barrier-honouring caller
_udo_cap_lazy = 0;       // the live entry is a sliced capture
_udo_cap_goal = 0;       // cells that capture must reach before the slot is free to write
_udo_cow_budget = UDO_COW_MIN;  // cells per barrier call; @block rescales from samplesblock.
                                // Non-zero from @init so a capture can never stall before
                                // the first block (swing_ldr_run pumps to completion inline).

// Reconciler ghost-discrimination state: each registry slot's heartbeat as of
// the PREVIOUS ~1Hz reconcile pass. A live duplicate's heartbeat advances
// between passes (@block rewrites it every block); a ghost's (a dead
// incarnation's leftover registry cells — gmem persists across reloads) is
// frozen. 16 = GS_INST_REG_MAX (literal: the constant is defined later in
// @init, and this MUST allocate before the s_audio_start slab below).
// freemem = session-volatile: zeroed on reinstantiation = the first-pass
// two-sighting guard (never duel on a single sighting).
_coll_hb_prev = freemem; freemem += 16;

// Comp link, two-way bookkeeping. Four cells per param id 1..9 (ids are
// 1-based, so cell 0 of each goes unused; 16 apiece keeps the slabs aligned
// with the one above and leaves room if the row ever carries more).
// To know WHO moved a control you have to remember what BOTH sides held last
// time you looked — that is the whole reason these exist. An echo that differs
// from the last echo means the folder's face was touched; a live value that
// differs from the last live value means this page was. Neither can be inferred
// from the other, and guessing is how a two-way link starts fighting itself.
_bcl_eprev = freemem; freemem += 16;   // echo as of the previous pass
_bcl_lprev = freemem; freemem += 16;   // our value as of the previous pass
_bcl_sent  = freemem; freemem += 16;   // value posted, while a post is in flight
_bcl_wait  = freemem; freemem += 16;   // 1 = our post is out and unconfirmed

// The same four again for the EON Tone link (EQ + drive). Thirteen params
// rather than nine; 16 apiece keeps every slab here the same width.
// Tone link: TNL_NPARAM params -- 13, plus the five master-EQ Q values of
// ser_ver 75. These four arrays are indexed by PARAM NUMBER, 1..TNL_NPARAM,
// so each needs TNL_NPARAM + 1 cells.
// ⚠️⚠️ They were a literal 16 -- enough for 13, not for 18 -- and
// _tnl_wait was then the LAST allocation before s_audio_start: params 16..18 would
// have written into the first samples of the first pad's audio, silently.
// Sized from the constant now, so the two cannot drift apart again.
TNL_NPARAM = 18;
TNL_Q_TRIES = 4;   // pushes of a Q param (14..18) with no echo before the peer counts as one that does not speak Q (2026-10-16)
_tnl_eprev = freemem; freemem += TNL_NPARAM + 1;
_tnl_lprev = freemem; freemem += TNL_NPARAM + 1;
_tnl_sent  = freemem; freemem += TNL_NPARAM + 1;
_tnl_wait  = freemem; freemem += TNL_NPARAM + 1;

// The step sequencer (rk_seq_core, Spec_Swing_Seq_View 6; phase S1 2026-10-19): the steps of every
// pattern, the lane and pattern records, the song chain, the per-lane walker state, the note-off
// schedule and a serialize scratch -- about 175 K cells at sixteen patterns, the LAST allocation before
// s_audio_start (it moves the pad pool up by that much; the headroom note below still holds). The inc
// claims nothing itself; seq_init takes the bases.
// SEQ_PATS + 1: the slot after the live patterns is the clipboard (SEQ_CLIP; S3, 2026-10-20)
_seq_m_step = freemem; freemem += (SEQ_PATS + 1) * SEQ_LANES * SEQ_STEPS * SEQ_ATTR;
_seq_m_lane = freemem; freemem += (SEQ_PATS + 1) * SEQ_LANES * SEQ_LANE_F;
_seq_m_pat  = freemem; freemem += (SEQ_PATS + 1) * SEQ_PAT_F;
_seq_m_song = freemem; freemem += SEQ_SONG_MAX * 2;
_seq_m_wk   = freemem; freemem += SEQ_LANES * SEQ_WK_F;
_seq_m_noq  = freemem; freemem += SEQ_NOQ_MAX * SEQ_NOQ_F;   // S6: four cells an entry (the mirror)
_seq_m_tmp  = freemem; freemem += 64;   // the serialize scratch: a dropped pattern's records (13 cells) and gate 79's SETTINGS block (32)
_seq_m_rsub = freemem; freemem += (SEQ_PATS + 1) * SEQ_LANES * SEQ_STEPS * SEQ_RSUB_N;   // the rolls' sub-velocities (phase S2; ~101 K cells with the clipboard)
_seq_m_opq  = freemem; freemem += SEQ_OPQ_N * 4;                                   // the op queue's ring (P0.0): @gfx posts, @block applies
// S5: the piano roll's notes (six slots of three cells per step, every lane and pattern and the clipboard: ~608 K cells,
// against the ~5 M headroom below) and the block's MIDI out (+1 entry: the sort's swap cell)
_seq_m_note = freemem; freemem += (SEQ_PATS + 1) * SEQ_LANES * SEQ_STEPS * SEQ_CHORD_N * SEQ_NOTE_F;
_seq_m_mo   = freemem; freemem += (SEQ_MO_CAP + 1) * 4;
_seq_m_hb   = freemem; freemem += (SEQ_HB_MAX + 1) * SEQ_HB_F;   // S5 (Codex): the walk's hits per block, sorted (+1: the swap cell)
_seq_m_io   = freemem; freemem += 2 * SEQ_IO_F;                   // S3c: the stream's two channels (the project file, the kit record)
_seq_m_meta = freemem; freemem += SEQ_PATS * SEQ_META_F;          // round two H: each pattern's own name (16 chars) and colour
seq_print_wk = freemem; freemem += SEQ_LANES * SEQ_WK_F;         // S6: the live walkers parked while a PRINT walks
_seq_m_echo = freemem; freemem += 256; seq_echo_on_t = _seq_m_echo; seq_echo_off_t = _seq_m_echo + 128;   // S6: when the mirror last sent each note's on / off (samples)
memset(_seq_m_echo, -1000000000, 256);
seq_init(_seq_m_step, _seq_m_lane, _seq_m_pat, _seq_m_song, _seq_m_wk, _seq_m_noq, _seq_m_tmp, _seq_m_rsub, _seq_m_opq, _seq_m_note, _seq_m_mo, _seq_m_hb, _seq_m_io);
seq_meta_init(_seq_m_meta);   // round two H: the names and colours block
_seq_m_mv = freemem; freemem += 32; seq_ui_mvtmp = _seq_m_mv;   // S5: a moved hit's cells in transit (the MOVE view)
seq_ui_rbase = _seq_m_mv + 16; memset(seq_ui_rbase, -1, 16);    // S5: each lane's roll window, its lowest row (-1: around the pad's root)
// ⚠ EON_SEQ_PLIST_MAX is DEFINED HERE, not with the band's other constants below: @init runs top to bottom and a constant
// read before its line is 0, so this claim took no cells and the region map's block began on the same address as the
// list's -- opening BROWSE wrote the list's indices over the map (the chips read patterns 3, 7, 11, 15; the region names
// came out as boxes; the song print walked the wrong patterns). The user found it 2026-10-21 (FINDINGS_LOG).
EON_SEQ_PLIST_MAX = 832;   // the preset list's rows at most (the band's: hdr +0 SEQ, +1 COUNT, +2 NGENRE; genres at +64 + g*24; entries at +1024 + i*48)
_seq_m_plist = freemem; freemem += EON_SEQ_PLIST_MAX;                              // the preset list's filtered indices (S3b; @gfx's)
seq_ui_plist_init(_seq_m_plist);
_seq_m_map = freemem; freemem += 512;                                             // the region map's mirror (S4): 64 x 4, the names at +256, the printed spans at +452 (the small-things round)
seq_map_init(_seq_m_map);
seq_ui_chgeo = freemem; freemem += 64;                                            // the small-things round: the song strip's chain chips (x, w per chip, 32 chips) for the face's hit-testing (rk_seq_ui; @gfx's)

// Audio buffers
s_audio_start = freemem;
// freemem += NUM_PADS * SLOT_SIZE;  -- do not advance; REAPER manages rest

// The allocator (banks step 2a, rk_swing_alloc): every slot starts with NO region, and a load
// takes what it needs from the AUDIO_AREA cells above s_audio_start at begin. The identity
// map of step 1a is gone; this line and _send_fx_mem are the only two places s_audio_start
// arithmetic may appear (the grep gate), and every reader goes through p_aptr / p_lptr.
// @serialize's read resets and refills the tables from the stream.
swing_alloc_init(s_audio_start, AUDIO_AREA);
swing_alloc_reset(NUM_SLOTS);
swing_disp_clear(_al_dl_blk); swing_disp_clear(_al_dl_srz);
// The four displaced lists the allocator's settle must count as live memory: a loader job's
// regions in flight (both lanes) and the two one-shot lists. ldr_job0 / ldr_job1 exist since
// swing_ldr_init above.
swing_alloc_register_dl(ldr_job0 + LDR_F_DISP); swing_alloc_register_dl(ldr_job1 + LDR_F_DISP);
swing_alloc_register_dl(_al_dl_blk);            swing_alloc_register_dl(_al_dl_srz);
// ...and the staged browser drop's region (2026-10-15): lane 0 only carries stream drops (rk_swing_padpcm)
swing_alloc_register_stage(ldr_job0 + LDR_F_STGP);
// The backing self-check (2026-09-23, rk_swing_alloc): distinct markers every ALLOC_BK_STEP over the
// pool AND the SEND_FX_RESERVE + 1M above it where the send FX, the swap chunk and the undo backup are about to be
// placed (before their inits, so the markers are theirs to overwrite), all read back at once. The
// first failing page becomes the pool's top; _mbk_top also bounds _udo_ready and _mem_head below,
// and alloc_backed = 0 puts the LCD's "memory short" notice up. A second pass runs at block 10.
_mbk_hi  = max(__memtop(), s_audio_start + AUDIO_AREA + SEND_FX_RESERVE + 1000000);   // the whole intended layout (+1M slack), or the grant if larger -- never the report alone
_mbk_top = swing_alloc_backing_scan(s_audio_start, _mbk_hi);
// Where the send FX begin = where the pool ends: the intended base, or lower on a machine whose
// backed top cannot hold the layout, so the FX, the swap chunk and the undo slot always sit under
// the backed top and only the pool gives. The grep gate for `s_audio_start +` allows exactly two
// lines: the probe bound above and this FX base -- the identity-map builder is gone.
_fx_base = min(s_audio_start + AUDIO_AREA, _mbk_top - SEND_FX_RESERVE);
_fx_base < alloc_end ? alloc_end = _fx_base;
_mbk_top < _mbk_hi ? alloc_backed = 0;

// ⚠️⚠️ HEADROOM BUDGET. Everything allocated ABOVE this line shares one budget
// with everything the plugin addresses past it. maxmem is 128,000,000, and on
// top of s_audio_start come, in order: the pad-audio pool (AUDIO_AREA = 104M),
// the send FX (delay, reverb, comp, Anvil tables), the swap chunk and the undo
// backup (UDO_VSLOT = 16M, one pad's four 45 s layers) -- about 18.5M of overhead
// inside SEND_FX_RESERVE = 19M, so ~5M of headroom under the 128M grant. Any new
// allocation up here pushes all of that higher, and past the BACKED top (the grant,
// or less on a machine short of memory) writes land in EEL2's shared dummy cell:
// same-frame readbacks succeed and NOTHING PERSISTS. That does not crash and does
// not warn. It presents as "kits stopped loading". Since 2026-09-23 the startup
// self-check (swing_alloc_backing_scan, right after the allocator init) measures
// that top; _mem_head/_mem_fits (the FX view's headroom readout) are measured
// against it where the last of it is allocated -- after the undo slot, beside _udo_ready.

// ─── Init per-pad defaults ────────────────────────────────────────────────
i = 0; loop(NUM_SLOTS,   // step 2b: every slot of every bank gets the defaults
  p_gain[i]    = 1.0;
  p_pan[i]     = 0.0;
  p_panL[i]    = 1.0;
  p_panR[i]    = 1.0;
  // The smoothers START at the coefficients, not at zero: a pad whose first
  // hit had to ramp up from silence would click exactly where it must not.
  p_panL_sm[i] = 1.0;
  p_panR_sm[i] = 1.0;
  p_tune[i]    = 0.0;
  // Per-layer baked-tune anchors (MAX_LAYERS per pad) all start at 0 = original.
  _bti = 0; loop(MAX_LAYERS, sp_baked_tune[i * MAX_LAYERS + _bti] = 0.0; _bti += 1;);
  p_attack[i]  = 0.5;   // near-instant for drums, minimal click
  p_decay[i]   = 2000;  // max decay — let the full sample ring out
  p_sustain[i] = 1.0;   // full sustain — sample plays through
  p_release[i] = 250;   // smooth release, avoids abrupt cutoff
  p_adsr_user[i] = 0;   // 0 = ADSR is auto-derived; flips to 1 when user touches knob/drag
  p_mute[i]    = 0;
  p_solo[i]    = 0;
  p_note[i]    = root_note + i;
  p_rng_lo[i]  = 0;   // single-note range = today's behavior
  p_rng_hi[i]  = 0;
  p_output[i]  = 0;
  p_note_lock[i] = 0;
  s_len[i]     = 0;
  s_start[i]   = 0;
  s_end[i]     = 1.0;
  s_skip[i]    = 0;
  s_norm[i]    = 0;
  s_norm_gain[i] = 1.0;
  s_dirty[i]   = 1;
  s_sr[i]      = 0;    // 0 = no sample loaded / unknown SR
  p_color[i]   = (i % NUM_PADS) / 16.0;  // default: evenly-spaced hues around the wheel, the same sixteen in every bank
  p_choke[i]   = 0;    // no choke group
  p_oneshot[i] = -1;   // -1 = follow global one-shot setting
  p_reverse[i] = 0;    // forward playback
  p_swapLR[i]  = 0;    // L↔R off (mono samples and most stereo files don't need it)
  // SP_PITCH state — explicit init. Cannot rely on freemem zero-init in
  // all reload scenarios; @serialize backfills these for ser_ver >= 45,
  // but a fresh instantiation with no project state will skip serialize
  // and inherit whatever bits the freemem allocator handed us. Without
  // explicit zeroing, the Extension's probe showed garbage doubles like
  // 1.97309e-153 / 3.72447e+213 propagating from sp_pitch_mode[i] into
  // the gmem control band via swing_block_pitch_tick.
  sp_pitch_mode[i]         = 0;      // Repitch (default)
  sp_pitch_algo[i]         = 0;      // Drum (default)
  // v3 stateless protocol: no JSFX-side shadows. swing_block_pitch_tick
  // blast-publishes mode/tune/algo every tick (and force-allocates the
  // named-segment block at @init), so there is nothing to seed here.
  p_layer_cnt[i] = 0;   // 0 = legacy single-layer mode (uses s_len/s_start/s_end directly)
  p_layer_mode[i] = 3;  // sum
  p_rr_idx[i] = 0;
  p_sum_tight[i] = 0;   // 0.0 = tight (no offset)
  p_rpt_div[i] = 0;     // 0 = OFF (follow global)
  p_rpt_ctr[i] = 0;
  p_rpt_swph[i] = 0;
  // FX defaults
  fx_hpf_freq[i] = 20;     // HPF off (below audible)
  fx_lpf_freq[i] = 20000;  // LPF off (above audible)
  fx_eq_lo[i]    = 0;      // EQ flat
  fx_eq_mid[i]   = 0;
  fx_eq_mid2[i]  = 0;
  fx_eq_hi[i]    = 0;
  fx_eq_lo_freq[i]  = 200;    // EQ low frequency default
  fx_eq_mid_freq[i] = 1000;   // EQ mid frequency default
  fx_eq_mid2_freq[i] = 3000;  // EQ hi-mid frequency default
  fx_eq_mid_q[i]  = 0.8;      // bell Q defaults (match the pre-v46 fixed 0.8)
  fx_eq_mid2_q[i] = 0.8;
  fx_eq_lo_q[i]   = 0.7071;   // shelf Q defaults (== the pre-v48 fixed S=1.0)
  fx_eq_hi_q[i]   = 0.7071;
  fx_eq_hi_freq[i]  = 5000;   // EQ high frequency default
  fx_sat_drv[i]  = 0;      // saturation off
  fx_drv_mode[i] = 0;      // drive mode: SOFT (default)
  fx_bc_rate[i]  = 0;      // bitcrush rate: 0 = off
  fx_bc_bits[i]  = 16;     // bitcrush depth: 16 = clean
  fx_snd_dly[i]  = 0;      // delay send: 0 = off
  fx_snd_rvb[i]  = 0;      // reverb send: 0 = off
  fx_snd_smash[i] = 0;     // smash send: 0 = off
  fx_cmp_amt[i]  = 0;      // compressor off
  fx_cmp_mode[i] = 0;      // default PUNCH
  fx_reso[i]     = 0.707;  // Butterworth Q (flat response)
  // FX filter state init
  fx_hpf_stL[i] = 0; fx_hpf_stR[i] = 0;
  fx_bc_cnt[i] = 0; fx_bc_holdL[i] = 0; fx_bc_holdR[i] = 0; fx_bc_lvl[i] = 32768;
  fx_lpf_stL[i] = 0; fx_lpf_stR[i] = 0;
  fx_cmp_env[i] = 0; fx_cmp_last_gr[i] = 0; fx_cmp_last_lin[i] = 1.0;
  // The 3.0.13 additions, explicitly zeroed for the same reason sp_pitch_mode
  // is twenty lines up: freemem is not reliably zero on every reload, and each
  // of these is READ before it is written on the first sample of a hit.
  //   fx_sat_drv_sm  is _drv, the wet/dry coefficient in `_aL += (_doL-_aL)*_drv`
  //                  -- garbage here is not a fast self-heal, it is one sample of
  //                  arbitrary magnitude arriving at the output guard.
  //   fx_res         is a COUNTDOWN. Garbage > 0 counts down one per sample, so a
  //                  large value holds every pad's whole FX chain awake for the
  //                  session -- the sleep gate silently off, which is the one
  //                  thing it was added to do.
  //   fx_dc_*        one stale offset through the 5 Hz blocker on the first
  //                  TUBE sample.
  // fx_sat_drv_sm starts at 0 and NOT at fx_sat_drv[i] only because the two are
  // the same thing here -- fx_sat_drv[i] was set to 0 thirty lines up, in this
  // same loop. Whatever @serialize restores after @init arrives later, and the
  // idle snap in process_pad_fx (which runs for every pad on every sample,
  // Swing_ReaKit.jsfx:5327) carries the smoother to it before the pad is struck.
  fx_res[i] = 0;
  fx_sat_drv_sm[i] = 0;
  fx_dc_x1L[i] = 0; fx_dc_y1L[i] = 0;
  fx_dc_x1R[i] = 0; fx_dc_y1R[i] = 0;
  i += 1;
);

// Init per-layer metadata
i = 0; loop(NUM_SLOTS,
  li = 0; loop(MAX_LAYERS,
    _lidx = i * MAX_LAYERS + li;
    l_len[_lidx] = 0;
    l_start[_lidx] = 0;
    l_end[_lidx] = 1.0;
    l_sr[_lidx] = 0;
    l_norm[_lidx] = 0;
    l_norm_gain[_lidx] = 1.0;
    l_vel_lo[_lidx] = li / MAX_LAYERS;        // default: even split
    l_vel_hi[_lidx] = (li + 1) / MAX_LAYERS;  // L1=0-0.25, L2=0.25-0.5, etc.
    l_rr_order[_lidx] = li;                    // default: L1→L2→L3→L4
    l_gain[_lidx] = 1.0;                        // unity gain
    strcpy(LPATH_STR_BASE + _lidx, "");         // init layer path string
    li += 1;
  );
  i += 1;
);

_syn_trig_ctr = 0;   // per-hit PRNG seed counter (session-volatile)
// SYN slot defaults (same pattern as l_* above: @serialize read overwrites)
i = 0; loop(NUM_SLOTS,
  ps_enable[i] = 0; ps_engine[i] = 0; ps_level[i] = 1;
  ps_vel_lo[i] = 0; ps_vel_hi[i] = 1; ps_rr_order[i] = MAX_LAYERS;
  ps_mac0[i] = 0.5; ps_mac1[i] = 0.5; ps_mac2[i] = 0.5; ps_mac3[i] = 0.5;
  ps_mac4[i] = 0.5; ps_mac5[i] = 0.5; ps_mac6[i] = 0.5; ps_mac7[i] = 0.5;
  i += 1;
);

i = 0; loop(V_SLOTS, v_pos[i] = -1; v_slot[i] = 0; v_stage[i] = 0; v_layer[i] = 0; v_kind[i] = 0; v_stfb[i] = 0; v_quiet[i] = 0; i += 1;);
memset(pad_flash, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
memset(p_peak, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
memset(p_peak_hold, 0, NUM_SLOTS);

memset(p_held, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
memset(p_held_vel, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
memset(_retrig_cd, 0, NUM_SLOTS);
memset(km_pad_vol_pan, 0, NUM_SLOTS * KM_PAD_MINI * KS);
memset(km_console, 0, NUM_SLOTS * KM_CON_PER_PAD * KS);

// Precomputed steal ramp (5ms fast fade) — computed once at init, valid for session
steal_coeff = exp(-1.0 / max(1, 0.005 * srate));
// SYN voice retirement. A synth voice has no sample end, and on a kit whose
// pads carry no `sustain` the ADSR never falls -- so the ONLY thing retiring
// it was the 3 s age cap, holding a slot for ~2.8 s after the drum went
// silent. With 16 slots, 16 hits in 3 s exhausted the pool and every hit
// after that stole an older voice. Retire on ACTUAL silence instead.
// Threshold is deliberately far below audibility and the hold deliberately
// long: a clap is several bursts with gaps, and cutting one short would be a
// far worse bug than a slot freed late. An engine that never decays below the
// threshold still falls back to the age cap.
SYN_QUIET_T = 0.00001;              // -100 dB
syn_quiet_n = 0.06 * srate;         // 60 ms of continuous silence
// Precomputed smoothing coefficients (sample-rate-independent)
_pad_meter_decay = exp(-1.0 / max(1, 0.090 * srate));   // ~90ms pad meter fall
_mst_meter_decay = exp(-1.0 / max(1, 0.450 * srate));   // ~450ms master meter fall
_sm_coeff = 1.0 - exp(-1.0 / max(1, 0.0045 * srate));   // ~4.5ms (sat drive + master vol)
_pad_sm_coeff = 1.0 - exp(-1.0 / max(1, 0.008 * srate));  // ~8ms (per-pad pan + drive)
// Browser audition release. LINEAR, not the one-pole the smoothers above use:
// this one has to actually REACH zero to end the voice, and a one-pole only
// approaches it. ~4 ms -- long enough to kill the step, short enough that STOP
// still feels instant.
_prv_fade_step = 1.0 / max(1, 0.004 * srate);
// UI font scale, recomputed every @gfx frame. Seeded to 1 so the two frames
// before gfx_w is trustworthy cannot produce a 0 and collapse every font.
_ui_sc = 1.0;
// Pad sleep-gate hold: how long a pad keeps processing after its chain last
// showed energy. Only has to bridge a zero crossing, so 30 ms is generous --
// and being derived from srate it is the same 30 ms at every rate.
_fx_hold_n = max(1, 0.030 * srate) | 0;
// TUBE DC blocker pole, y = x - x1 + R*y1. ~5 Hz: below the lowest drum
// fundamental worth keeping, high enough to settle in a few tens of ms.
_dc_r = exp(-2 * $pi * 5.0 / max(1, srate));
last_srate = srate;

_prev_play_state = 0;  // transport state tracker for retrigger reset
_transport_grace = 0;  // note-off suppression counter after transport start
_xf_active = 0;           // anti-pop crossfade: not active until deserialize

// ─── Master idle gate (Phase 4, A O-1, 2026-09-15; the gate is decided at the end
//     of @block, the skip is in @sample) ────────────────────────────────────────
_mst_idle = 0;        // 1 = @sample skips the master section (re-checked per sample with voices_alive)
_mst_quiet_n = 0;     // samples since anything last reached the bus (capped at 4 s)
_any_stretch = 0;     // per block: some pad is in Stretch mode (gates the ring drain)
_mst_live = 0; _mst_idle_want = 0; _mst_pi = 0;
_dly_inL = 0; _dly_inR = 0; _rvb_inL = 0; _rvb_inR = 0;
// IDENT name publish (Phase 4, A O-3): the band is compared against the strings only on
// heal blocks (every 64th, and on a slot change); otherwise one strcmp per pad
_id_pub_slot = -1; _id_heal = 0; _id_sh = 0;
_xf_pos = 0;
_xf_len = 1;
memset(_xf_prev, 0, OUT_PAIRS * 2);  // no previous output at init (every pin)
out_nch = OUT_CH_BASE;    // @block's routing pass sets it before every @sample; this is only the floor
_coll_last_check = time_precise();  // avoid spurious reconciliation on first @block

// ─── GUI state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
overlay_pad  = -1;   // which pad has the per-pad EDITOR open (-1 = none, 0..NUM_PADS-1)
rng_ov_pad   = -1;   // which pad has the KEY-RANGE overlay open (right-click RANGE pill; -1 = none)
kmac_ed_open = 0;    // kit-macro EDITOR overlay (MACRO tab EDIT ▸ chip; 0 = closed)
pk_ov_pad    = -1;   // which pad has the NOTE picker open (click the NOTE pill; -1 = none)
pk_reframe   = 0;    // 1 = an opener wants the per-KIT open framing recomputed (see notepick)
cat_ov_pad   = -1;   // which pad has the CATEGORY glyph-grid overlay open (§9c; badge/pill RMB; -1 = none)
_co_lastpad  = -1;   // category-overlay fresh-frame guard: JSFX default 0 would false-match pad 0's first open
// ── Big View framework ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A "big view" is a modal page that takes over the pad-grid rect (input-gated,
// close owned per-view). big_view_id (0 = none) is the framework discriminator,
// kept SEPARATE from overlay_pad (the per-pad editor index) so neither var is
// overloaded. Only one modal class is active at a time. Session-transient —
// never serialized. Input policy lives in pad_input_allowed() (state lib).
VIEW_NONE    = 0;
VIEW_CONSOLE = 1;    // full-size mixer/console over the grid (was OVERLAY_MIXER==99)
VIEW_MAPPING = 2;    // note-assignment + choke map (rk_swing_ui_mapping.jsfx-inc)
VIEW_COLORS  = 3;    // per-pad hue board (rk_swing_ui_colors.jsfx-inc)
VIEW_OUTPUTS = 4;    // pad → bus routing matrix (rk_swing_ui_outputs.jsfx-inc)
VIEW_EQ      = 5;    // full-size master EQ curve editor (swing_panels_draw_eq_big)
VIEW_DELAY   = 6;    // full-size delay page (swing_panels_draw_fx_big 2)
VIEW_REVERB  = 7;    // full-size reverb page (swing_panels_draw_fx_big 3)
VIEW_COMP    = 8;    // full-size compressor page (swing_panels_draw_fx_big 5)
VIEW_KITS    = 9;    // LOAD-button kit browser (rk_swing_ui_kitsview.jsfx-inc)
VIEW_SYNTH   = 10;   // per-pad drum-synth editor (rk_swing_ui_synthview.jsfx-inc)
VIEW_FXPICK  = 11;   // FX picker, full-window (rk_swing_ui_fxview.jsfx-inc)
                     // ⚠️ ADDING A VIEW? Four sites, and the third is SILENT:
                     //   1. this constant
                     //   2. the dispatch chain in @gfx
                     //   3. the EON_VIEW_REQ ceiling (VIEW_ID_MAX) — it drops any id
                     //      above it with NO error, so the view opens by click
                     //      and stays invisible to Lua, actions and the toolbar.
                     //      Raise it in the SAME commit as the id.
                     //   4. a Scripts/EON_View_*.lua calling T.view(id)
big_view_id  = VIEW_NONE;
// Pad Banks step 4d: the BANK ACTIONS ride the same mailbox -- they are not views. 12..15 show bank A..D (the
// selection keeps its tile), 16 / 17 the next / previous bank (both wrap). swing_banktabs_select: mark_dirty,
// never an undo boundary. Scripts EON_Swing_Bank_A/B/C/D/Next/Prev.lua (eon_action_target T.view).
VIEW_BANK_A    = 12;
VIEW_BANK_B    = 13;
VIEW_BANK_C    = 14;
VIEW_BANK_D    = 15;
VIEW_BANK_NEXT = 16;
VIEW_BANK_PREV = 17;
VIEW_SEQ       = 18;   // the step sequencer's grid, full-window (rk_seq_ui.jsfx-inc; Spec_Swing_Seq_View 7.3, phase S1)
VIEW_ID_MAX    = 18;   // the EON_VIEW_REQ ceiling: an id above it is dropped -- raise it with any new id
syn_view_pad = 0;    // SYNTH view's edit target (session-transient)

// ─── Console strip sections (P5) ───────────────────────────────────────────
// Which bands the console draws, and how tall each one is. The FADER is the
// only flex element in the strip — every other section is a fixed height, so
// whatever is switched off the fader absorbs. That is what makes these cheap.
//
// ⚠️ Every toggle is a BAND across all 16 strips, never per-strip. Sections
// change strip HEIGHT, and two strips of different height get faders of
// different LENGTH — the same mouse travel would be a different number of dB
// on each channel and 0 dB would sit at a different height on every one. The
// focus strip is the deliberate exception and it only spends WIDTH.
//
// Defaults are state "B" (the FX rack): inserts open at 8 slots, Swing's fixed
// chain folded to its summary bar, everything else on.
//
// ⚠️ ONE-SHOT GUARD, not a plain assignment. These are serialized, so a bare
// `con_ins = 1` here would reset the user's choices on any @init that runs
// after a project load without @serialize running behind it.
//   new instance   → defaults below stand
//   project load   → defaults, then @serialize read overwrites them
//   re-init        → skipped entirely, the loaded values survive
//
// ⚠️⚠️ THE REASON THIS USED TO GIVE WAS WRONG, and it is worth not repeating:
// it said "a sample-rate change re-runs @init WITHOUT re-running @serialize".
// MEASURED 2026-08-03 (sandboxed 7.78, an @init-counter gmem cell, and
// mutation-verified by forcing ext_noinit = 0 in a probe copy, which DID re-run
// every time): with ext_noinit = 1 a samplerate flip does NOT re-run @init at
// all. ext_noinit shields samplerate re-inits as well as play-start ones. See
// wiki 3.2, which names that premise as wrong on stock 7.78.
//
// ⭐ THE GUARD STAYS ANYWAY, and the reason is better than the old one: that
// shield is UNDOCUMENTED behaviour and can drift between REAPER versions. A
// guard that costs one compare is the right price for not depending on it. Note
// what the guard is protecting against is therefore hypothetical today -- but
// the per-pad @init loop and swing_apply_defaults_* have no such guard, so if
// the shield ever does drift, THEY are where it lands, not here.
// ⚠️ The measurement is on 7.78 and the field is on 7.80, and the ss_srwipe
// harness that produced it no longer exists. Re-measure before relying on it.
// The backfill in the ser_ver 58 gate covers pre-58 projects separately; it
// cannot cover a brand new instance, which is why both exist.
_con_defaults_done ? 0 : (
  con_ins      = 1;  // inserts band present
  con_ins_full = 1;  // 1 = slot cards · 0 = one-line summary bar
  con_ins_house = 0; // 1 = the pad rows also show the house plugins (Drum Strip, Macros); 0 = only what the user added
  con_slots    = 8;  // 4 / 6 / 8, or 0 = FIT (as many as the column allows)
  con_sw       = 1;  // Swing's own HPF/LPF/EQ/CMP/BIT/DRV band present
  con_sw_full  = 1;  // 1 = six labelled rows · 0 = summary bar. Open by default
                     // (2026-09-09): the band IS the channel's own EQ/dynamics
                     // and a fresh desk that hides it reads as if the pad has no
                     // processing of its own.
  con_sends    = 1;  // DLY / RVB / SMS rotaries
  con_pan      = 1;
  con_cut      = 1;  // solo / mute / rec row
  con_fader    = 1;
  con_meter    = 1;
  con_dbsc     = 1;  // dB scale inside the fader well
  con_name     = 1;  // scribble strip
  con_focus    = 0;  // selected channel drawn WIDE (not taller) -- same
                     // height and same sections as every other strip, so
                     // the faders still share one zero and one throw.
  con_master   = 1;  // master strip on the right. ON by default (2026-09-09,
                     // user): a console without its master reads as a fragment.
                     // con_ins_house stays 0 beside it -- the pad rows show what
                     // YOU added, not Swing's own house plugins.
  // Desk finish. 0 = the blue the console has always been, so zero-init IS
  // the old look. Finishes, not a colour picker: a desk has a finish, and 16
  // strips of hardware read as one object only while the ground behind them
  // stays a single considered surface.
  con_bg       = 5;  // 0 blue · 1 graphite · 2 black · 3 slate · 4 walnut· 5 light
                     // Light is the shipped finish from 2026-09-09. The blue is
                     // still there as finish 0; every project that already chose
                     // one keeps it (con_bg is serialized, and this block only
                     // runs for a genuinely new instance).
  con_wf       = 0;  // fader well fill: 0 full slab · 1 thin colour edge · 2 off
  // Insert-band viewport offset, ONE for all sixteen strips. Deliberately NOT
  // serialized: it is where you are looking, not what the project is. It is
  // re-clamped every frame against the band that actually fits, and reset to
  // 0 whenever there is nothing to scroll.
  con_ins_scroll = 0;
  // FX LCD: show REAPER's track number beside the target name. Lives here
  // rather than at @init because it is SERIALIZED — the one-time guard is what
  // stops a sample-rate change (which re-runs @init) from wiping the choice.
  // The ser_ver < 60 backfill covers OLD projects; this covers NEW instances,
  // which no backfill can reach.
  fxv_tnum_on = 1;
  fxv_vend_on = 1;   // same two-defaults rule as fxv_tnum_on above
  fxv_cats_open = 1; // rail categories start OPEN -- a fresh install must not
                     // look like the categories are missing
  // ⭐ REAPER's group starts FOLDED, and ours does not. Both open is a very
  // long rail, and ours is the vocabulary this instrument is built around --
  // REAPER's is the second opinion you go looking for. Folded is not hidden:
  // the header is right there with its count on it.
  fxv_rcat_open = 0;
  fxv_fold_open = 1; // YOUR folders start open -- they are the shortest group
  // No group starts hidden: hiding is a choice you make, never a default you
  // have to discover and undo.
  fxv_g2_off = 0; fxv_g3_off = 0; fxv_g4_off = 0;
                     // and the most personal, so folding them by default would
                     // hide the thing you made on purpose
  _con_defaults_done = 1;
);
// ─── Compact FX picker, over the console ─────────────────────────────────
// Clicking an empty insert slot used to open the FULL-WINDOW picker, which
// replaced the desk: you picked a plugin and were left in the browser, having
// to close it to get back to the channel you were working on. For "add one
// plugin to channel 7" that is a large context switch for a small act.
//
// This opens OVER the console instead, anchored near the slot you clicked, and
// closes itself on the pick. Session-transient -- a picker that was open when
// you saved should not be open when you load.
con_pick_open  = 0;  // 1 = the compact picker is up
con_pick_pad   = 0;  // pad it is aimed at (16 = the master strip)
con_pick_ap    = 0;  // ...and the SLOT that strip showed when it was clicked (its header names it)
con_pick_slot  = 0;  // chain slot it will land in
con_pick_fill  = 0;  // was that slot FILLED? swap if so, insert if not
con_pick_x     = 0;  // anchored to the slot, clamped inside the console
con_pick_y     = 0;
con_pick_scroll = 0;

con_opt_open = 0;    // gear panel — session-transient, NOT serialized, and
                     // deliberately unguarded: an SR change should close it.
tau = 2 * $pi;       // constant for arc/knob drawing
overlay_layer = 0;   // which layer is being displayed in overlay
active_id    = -1;
prev_LMB     = 0;
prev_RMB     = 0;
last_mouse_cap = 0;
// ── Per-surface press latches (D-3, Audit D 2026-09-14) ─────────────────────
// One prev_LMB used to serve every @gfx surface. REAPER 7.79 runs at most one
// window-or-embed surface of an instance at a time (EON_Probe_Surface S1-S6),
// with one exception: an instance embedded in BOTH the TCP and the MCP with its
// window closed, whose two embeds alternate pass for pass (S5: 88 passes and 88
// canvas-width flips in 2 s). REAPER hands an unhovered embed a mouse_cap of 0
// (EON_Weld's measurement), so while a pad was held in one embed the other's
// pass wrote prev_LMB = 0, and every following pass of the held embed saw a
// fresh press edge: the pad retriggered at the pass rate (~21/s), the embed VOL
// knob's drag ended and re-anchored every pass, and each phantom edge pushed an
// undo entry.
// So the latch is PER SURFACE -- EON_Weld's idiom (ebc_ck0 / ebc_ck1),
// extended to two embeds. Slot 0 is the window and the idle context: they never
// run together, and the idle canvas IS the window's. Slots 1 and 2 are the two
// embeds, told apart by canvas signature (gfx_w, gfx_h: 277 and 82 px wide in
// the rig); a signature nobody holds takes the slot the last embed pass did not
// use, so two alternating embeds settle into one slot each and a resized single
// embed simply re-keys.
// swing_srf_load (the @gfx head) puts this pass's latch into prev_LMB/prev_RMB,
// so the release and commit code keep reading prev_LMB unchanged;
// swing_srf_store (the frame tail) writes mouse_cap back into the same latch.
// A press belongs to the surface that saw its edge, until that surface sees the
// release. While the OTHER embed holds one, this embed's pass (no button, the
// pointer over the other panel) presents the press as still held at the owner's
// pointer and with the owner's modifiers, and no edge: the held pad is neither
// released nor re-launched, and a knob drag keeps its anchor instead of ending
// on every other pass (ssl_knob_interact ends a drag on any pass with LMB 0).
// The modifiers matter as much as the button: the same knob reads CTRL as its
// fine mode, so a Ctrl fine-drag handed a bare mouse_cap 0 computed every other
// pass at ten times the step (second audit, 2026-09-15). Bounded: the owner
// must have run within the last half second, or its press is over and its latch
// is dropped -- a hold can never outlive its surface.
// A window or idle pass is never frozen. It re-reads the physical button, and
// it first adopts every embed latch, so a press that began in an embed ends
// there as a release edge (undo commit, held-pad release), never as a new
// press. An embed pass drops the window latch the same way: an embed only runs
// while no window of the instance shows, so a press the window held is over.
_srf = 0; _srf_last_emb = 0; _srf_foreign = 0; _srf_cap = 0;
_srf_sig1 = 0; _srf_sig2 = 0; _srf_cap1 = 0; _srf_cap2 = 0;
_srf_plmb0 = 0; _srf_prmb0 = 0;
_srf_plmb1 = 0; _srf_prmb1 = 0; _srf_mx1 = 0; _srf_my1 = 0; _srf_t1 = 0;
_srf_plmb2 = 0; _srf_prmb2 = 0; _srf_mx2 = 0; _srf_my2 = 0; _srf_t2 = 0;

function swing_srf_load()
  local(_sg, _oth_plmb, _oth_prmb, _oth_mx, _oth_my, _oth_t, _oth_cap)
(
  // This pass's effective mouse_cap for the modifiers (the head reads CTRL,
  // SHIFT and ALT from it): the real one, unless a foreign press is handed over.
  _srf_cap = mouse_cap;
  is_embedded ? (
    _sg = gfx_w * 65536 + gfx_h;
    _srf = _sg == _srf_sig1 ? 1 : _sg == _srf_sig2 ? 2 : 0;
    _srf == 0 ? (
      _srf = _srf_last_emb == 1 ? 2 : 1;
      _srf == 1 ? ( _srf_sig1 = _sg; _srf_plmb1 = 0; _srf_prmb1 = 0; _srf_t1 = 0; _srf_cap1 = 0; )
                : ( _srf_sig2 = _sg; _srf_plmb2 = 0; _srf_prmb2 = 0; _srf_t2 = 0; _srf_cap2 = 0; );
    );
    _srf_last_emb = _srf;
    _srf_plmb0 = 0; _srf_prmb0 = 0;
    _srf == 1 ? (
      prev_LMB = _srf_plmb1; prev_RMB = _srf_prmb1;
      _oth_plmb = _srf_plmb2; _oth_prmb = _srf_prmb2;
      _oth_mx = _srf_mx2; _oth_my = _srf_my2; _oth_t = _srf_t2; _oth_cap = _srf_cap2;
    ) : (
      prev_LMB = _srf_plmb2; prev_RMB = _srf_prmb2;
      _oth_plmb = _srf_plmb1; _oth_prmb = _srf_prmb1;
      _oth_mx = _srf_mx1; _oth_my = _srf_my1; _oth_t = _srf_t1; _oth_cap = _srf_cap1;
    );
    (_oth_plmb || _oth_prmb) && time_precise() - _oth_t > 0.5 ? (
      // The owner has not run for half a second: its press is over.
      _srf == 1 ? ( _srf_plmb2 = 0; _srf_prmb2 = 0; ) : ( _srf_plmb1 = 0; _srf_prmb1 = 0; );
      _oth_plmb = 0; _oth_prmb = 0;
    );
    _srf_foreign = (_oth_plmb || _oth_prmb) && !(mouse_cap & 3);
    _srf_foreign ? (
      LMB = _oth_plmb; RMB = _oth_prmb;
      prev_LMB = _oth_plmb; prev_RMB = _oth_prmb;   // held, and no edge either way
      mx = _oth_mx; my = _oth_my;
      _srf_cap = _oth_cap;                          // ...with its modifiers
    );
  ) : (
    _srf = 0; _srf_foreign = 0;
    prev_LMB = _srf_plmb0 || _srf_plmb1 || _srf_plmb2;
    prev_RMB = _srf_prmb0 || _srf_prmb1 || _srf_prmb2;
    _srf_plmb1 = 0; _srf_prmb1 = 0; _srf_plmb2 = 0; _srf_prmb2 = 0;
  );
);

function swing_srf_store()
(
  _srf == 1 ? (
    _srf_plmb1 = mouse_cap & 1; _srf_prmb1 = mouse_cap & 2;
    _srf_foreign ? 0 : ( _srf_mx1 = mouse_x; _srf_my1 = mouse_y; _srf_t1 = time_precise(); _srf_cap1 = mouse_cap; );
  ) : _srf == 2 ? (
    _srf_plmb2 = mouse_cap & 1; _srf_prmb2 = mouse_cap & 2;
    _srf_foreign ? 0 : ( _srf_mx2 = mouse_x; _srf_my2 = mouse_y; _srf_t2 = time_precise(); _srf_cap2 = mouse_cap; );
  ) : (
    _srf_plmb0 = mouse_cap & 1; _srf_prmb0 = mouse_cap & 2;
  );
  prev_LMB = mouse_cap & 1;
  prev_RMB = mouse_cap & 2;
);
gfx_frame_count = 0;
frame_last_timer = 0;
any_solo     = 0;
// Apply factory defaults for serialized vars (see rk_swing_defaults.jsfx-inc).
// ext_noinit=1.0 makes @init one-shot per instance — @serialize overwrites
// these on project load; old presets backfill via `is_read && ser_ver < N`.
swing_apply_defaults_modes();
swing_apply_defaults_fx();
midi_learn_pad = -1; // pad waiting for MIDI learn (-1 = off)
gui_held_pad   = -1; // pad held by mouse click (-1 = none)
// SYN view: the 3D drum's strike animation. A TIMESTAMP + velocity, not a
// per-frame decay -- a frame-counted one ran at whatever rate the FX window
// redrew (0.28 s at 60 fps, 0.85 s at 20) and froze mid-decay whenever the
// view closed. Not p_held: see rk_swing_ui_synthview (a held repeat would drag
// the sample layer into a synth-only hit).
sv_d3_hit_t    = 0;  // time_precise() of the last strike
sv_d3_hit_v    = 0;  // its velocity, 0..1
SV_D3_HIT_SEC  = 0.10;  // squash envelope length
SV_D3_LIT_SEC  = 0.05;  // batter-head flash: SHORTER, because `lit` is a hard
                        // boolean in the renderer and cannot ease out
drag_src_pad   = -1; // source pad for drag-swap (-1 = no drag)
drag_active    = 0;  // 1 = currently dragging a pad
xdrag_last_stamp = 0;  // EON_DRAG: last request stamp seen from the browser
xdrag_seen_t   = 0;  // our own time_precise() when that stamp last changed
xdrag_last_slot = -2; // slot the shadow above belongs to (-2 = never observed;
                      // forces adopt-don't-trust on the first @gfx frame, since
                      // gmem outlives @init and a leftover stamp is not news)
xdrag_pad      = -1; // pad the browser's drag is currently over (-1 = none)
drag_start_x   = 0;  // mouse x at drag start
drag_start_y   = 0;  // mouse y at drag start
rpt_counter  = 0;    // sample counter for repeat timing
// rpt_grid (note repeat locked to the project grid) is @serialize'd and is
// deliberately NOT reset here: @init also runs on a sample-rate change, with
// no serialize read behind it, so a reset would silently drop the setting.
// EEL2 zero-init already gives the default, OFF.
RPT_GRID_GRACE = 0.30;  // a pad struck within this fraction of a step of the
                        // next grid line does not ALSO repeat on it -- that
                        // would flam against the player's own hit.
rpt_swing_phase = 0; // alternates 0/1 each repeat tick
// ─── Master output meter state ──────────────────────────────────────────
master_meterL = 0; master_meterR = 0;
master_gr_meter = 1.0;  // gain reduction meter for limiter

// ─── Jog wheel state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ─── Waveform zoom state ────────────────────────────────────────────────
wf_zoom     = 1.0;  // 1.0 = full view, 2.0 = 2x zoom, etc.
wf_scroll   = 0.0;  // normalized scroll position (0–1) within zoomed view
wf_snap_zc  = 1;    // 1 = snap trim markers to zero crossings

// Double-click tracking for LCD and overlay nodes
_dbl_click_time = 0;
_dbl_click_id = -1;
// Double-click tracking for MIX tab sliders
_mix_dbl_time = 0;
_mix_dbl_id = -1;
// ─── Kit Export/Import state machine ──────────────────────────────────────
// gmem layout constants
// RELOCATED 2026-07-09 from cells 0..35: a foreign in-process writer
// (control-surface extension family; per-boot segment-attach lottery)
// tramples absolute cells 0/1/2 of whichever segment it lands on
// ([0]=fader float, [1]=time_precise clock, [2]=const). On
// Swing_Media_Transfer that stomped CMD/VER/NPADS: kit loads jammed and a
// garbage VER mid-import produced the phantom-pad-16 pad-0 poison
// (project_strip_sync_pad0_stomp, ab36056). Now in the protected 2609xxxx
// band. Cells 0..35 are DEAD — never claim them. Keep in sync with
// rk_lua_core.lua GMEM (CMD/PARAM1-3/KIT_GMEM_VER/NPADS/NAMELEN/NAME_BASE)
// and Swing Lite rk_lite_core.jsfx-inc.
KIT_GMEM_CMD         = 26090300;  // command flag
KIT_GMEM_VER         = 26090301;  // format version (kit-import protocol)
KIT_GMEM_PARAM1      = 26090301;  // generic CMD parameter (e.g. pad index for
                              // CMD 50/51 rename). Same slot as
                              // KIT_GMEM_VER — they're polymorphic by
                              // protocol: KIT_GMEM_VER during kit-import
                              // (CMD 3), KIT_GMEM_PARAM1 elsewhere. The
                              // LOCK + CMD ordering guarantees the two
                              // uses never overlap in time.
KIT_GMEM_NPADS       = 26090302;  // number of pads (PARAM2 on the command bus)
KIT_GMEM_NAMELEN     = 26090303;  // kit name length (PARAM3 on the command bus).
                              // ⚠ ALIAS HAZARD: CMD 65/67 pass audio length
                              // here and CMD 66 returns a sample rate — an
                              // audio value transiently occupies the name-
                              // length cell. Safe ONLY because name reads
                              // happen inside the CMD-3 import window, time-
                              // separated by the CMD channel. Never add a
                              // consumer that reads the kit name outside an
                              // import. Also: CMD 65/66/67 use KIT_GMEM_AUDIO
                              // offset 0, where VER-201 kit staging puts pad
                              // 0's path string — all three defer on kit_busy
                              // + the bridge's CMD==0 send gate keeps them
                              // out of load windows.
KIT_GMEM_NAME        = 26090304;  // kit name chars (32 max, ..26090335)
// ── Kit-load transaction band 26090336..26090341 (claimed 2026-07-17;
// 341 claimed 2026-07-20 — band now full). Bridge stamps EPOCH before each dispatch;
// the consuming instance captures it at arm time and echoes +epoch at
// import completion (state 4) or -epoch on a 98 abort, plus instance_id
// and pad_fail_bits — a real completion ack for the bridge instead of
// watching the shared CMD cell. Keep in sync with rk_lua_core.lua GMEM.
GS_LOAD_EPOCH        = 26090336;  // bridge → JSFX: monotonic dispatch id; Phase 1b: ALSO
                                  // the arm signal (stamped LAST at dispatch — see gate)
GS_LOAD_ACK          = 26090337;  // JSFX → bridge: +epoch landed / -epoch aborted
GS_LOAD_ACK_INST     = 26090338;  // JSFX → bridge: instance_id that consumed the load
GS_LOAD_ACK_FAILBITS = 26090339;  // JSFX → bridge: pad_fail_bits after import (0 = clean)
GS_LOAD_WANT         = 26090340;  // requester → bridge: declared target for the NEXT
                                  // request (split off PENDING — see rk_lua_core.lua)
GS_DEV_BUTTON_LOAD   = 26090341;  // RETIRED 2026-08-03 (was: headless LOAD-button press).
                                  // The consumer is gone — it replayed a write-set the
                                  // LOAD button no longer uses, and a bare instance_id
                                  // trigger sat one cell above GS_LOAD_WANT's writers.
                                  // Cell stays reserved: NEVER reuse a cell a shipped
                                  // build has written. Headless LOAD = kitsview devpick.
GS_EXPORT_OVER       = 26090343;  // JSFX → bridge: 1 = the state-11 audio dump stopped at
                                  // the export band's ceiling (KIT_GMEM_AUDIO_DUMP_END) —
                                  // the kit holds more audio than the band carries, so
                                  // the bridge refuses the save instead of writing a
                                  // short kit. Written every dump, read at CMD 1 / 84.
                                  // Claimed 2026-09-08 (Spec_Swing_Long_Pad_Layer_Cap).
GS_KIT_EXPORT_BANK   = 26090344;  // bridge → JSFX: the bank (0..3) the next state-11 kit-export dump
                                  // publishes into the sixteen-wide bands + the audio dump. 0 = bank A =
                                  // the pre-banks behaviour. Pad Banks step 3b (2026-09-23).
GS_KIT_LOAD_BANK     = 26090345;  // bridge → JSFX: bank + 16 * wipe_mask for the next kit-import pass;
                                  // latched + zeroed at the state-1 arm (rk_swing_ui_state). Step 3b.
GS_KIT_LOAD_INTO     = 26090346;  // JSFX → bridge: bank + 1 = the NEXT requested kit's bank A lands in that bank
                                  // only (one pass, no follow-ups, no wipe); 0 = the whole instrument. Written
                                  // before CMD 24, consumed by the bridge's kit-request pickup. Step 4c (2026-09-23).
GS_KIT_EXPORT_ONLY   = 26090347;  // JSFX → bridge: bank + 1 = the save writes that ONE bank as a one-bank kit (the
                                  // bridge points GS_KIT_EXPORT_BANK at it for the dump, skips the walk, republishes
                                  // bank A); 0 = the whole instrument. Written before CMD 10 / the dev export. Step 4c.
// Seed the arm gate's epoch EDGE tracker with the session's current value so a
// freshly-(re)instantiated instance doesn't see a phantom edge on its first
// @block (stale nonzero epoch vs zero-initialized tracker).
kit_epoch_seen = gmem[GS_LOAD_EPOCH];
KIT_GMEM_GLOBALS     = 40;    // global settings (slots 40–89)
KIT_GMEM_META        = 100;   // pad metadata (80 per pad)
KIT_GMEM_META_PP     = 80;    // floats per pad in metadata
KIT_GMEM_PADNAMES    = 1720;  // pad name strings (32 chars per pad, 1720–2231)
KIT_GMEM_PADNAME_LEN = 32;
GS_PAD_OFFSET_BASE   = 2232;  // per-pad sample offset (16 floats, 2232–2247)
// Per-pad chromatic key-range, PACKED lo*128+hi (both 0..127 semitone offsets
// from p_note). One float per pad, 16 slots. RELOCATED 2026-07-08 from 2620:
// the old comment claimed "2620-2648 free" but FOUR owned GS cells live there
// (GS_PROJ_DIRTY 2620, GS_PAD_TRACK_SELECT 2623, GS_REAIMGUI_MISSING 2624,
// GS_FX_SEL_PAD 2625 — defined ~200 lines below in this same file). Every
// mark_dirty gave pad 0 a phantom range; range publishes ate the flags and
// snapped PadFX's selected pad. New home = the verified-free gap after
// GS_FX_PUB (26090000-63) and GS_STRIP_REINIT_PULSE (26090100). Keep in
// sync with rk_lua_core.lua GMEM.GS_PAD_RANGE_BASE.
GS_PAD_RANGE_BASE    = 26090200;  // ..26090215
// Per-pad smash-send kit overflow (KIT_GMEM_META's 80-float stride is FULL —
// see the GS_PAD_OFFSET_BASE note; same precedent as GS_PAD_RANGE_BASE).
// MUST match rk_lua_core.lua GS_PAD_SMASH_BASE.
GS_PAD_SMASH_BASE    = 26090240;  // ..26090255
// The bake anchors of the bank a state-11 dump publishes (2026-10-10): + tile * MAX_LAYERS + layer = sp_baked_tune
// (0 = the buffer is the pad's own audio; else it is a Tuned bake at that many semitones). A save would otherwise
// store a bake beside its tune and a reload pitch it twice (FINDINGS_LOG 2026-10-09). The STAMP = bank + 1 and the
// STAMP's ID = this instance_id, written last: the bridge takes them only for the instance it is saving and zeroes
// the stamp once read, so a dump that never writes them (Swing Lite) reads "none".
// MUST match rk_lua_core.lua GS_KIT_EXPORT_ANCHOR / _STAMP / _ID.
GS_KIT_EXPORT_ANCHOR       = 26090120;  // ..26090183
GS_KIT_EXPORT_ANCHOR_STAMP = 26090184;
GS_KIT_EXPORT_ANCHOR_ID    = 26090185;
GS_SYN_META_BASE     = 26090400;  // ..26090623 — SYN slot publish/stage, pad×14
                                  // (enable, engine, level, vel_lo, vel_hi,
                                  // rr_order, mac0..7); registered in
                                  // .refs/swing_gmem_bridge_protocol.md §3
GS_SYN_META_PP       = 14;
GS_SYN_STAGED_OFF    = 224;       // GS_SYN_META_BASE+224 = bridge-staged flag
                                  // (set by the bridge after staging kit synth
                                  // data; consumed by the import tick)
KIT_GMEM_AUDIOLEN    = 2256;  // audio length per pad (16 entries)
KIT_GMEM_AUDIO       = 3000;  // audio data start
// ── CMD-86 dedicated staging band (P3 migration path rewrite) ────────────
// 26300000..26320807, claimed 2026-07-12 (26200011..26499999 swept empty;
// HS control band starts at 26500000). The legacy staging home — the
// KIT_GMEM_AUDIO 260-cell band — is a SCRATCH BUS (block_pitch streams pad
// PCM over it for Extension bake capture right after project open), so
// CMD-86 payloads staged there were stomped before this consume read them.
// Two writers only: bridge stages paths, this JSFX echoes the adopted
// count into GS_MIGR_ADOPTED before the CMD ack (bridge presets -1 and
// retries when the echo comes back short). Keep in sync with
// rk_lua_core.lua GMEM.MIGR_*.
GS_MIGR_ADOPTED      = 26300000;             // +0 header: adopted-count echo
GS_MIGR_PAD_CELLS    = 26300008;             // + pad*260 (len-prefixed)
GS_MIGR_LAYER_CELLS  = GS_MIGR_PAD_CELLS + NUM_PADS * 260;  // + (pad*MAX_LAYERS+L)*260
// ── P4 step 3 REB bands (26320808..26342127, claimed 2026-07-15 from the
// same verified-free sweep, directly above the MIGR band).
// PUBLISH band (CMD-87 response): this JSFX copies its LIVE pad/layer path
// strings + lengths + layer counts + the pad_fail_bits bitmap here ON
// REQUEST, so the bridge can audit disk health / auto-rebase after a
// project move. The bridge has no other trustworthy source on a cold
// reopen: the pad_path_N ExtState breadcrumbs are staging-time-only and
// session-global (stale/foreign after reopen), and the KIT_GMEM_AUDIO
// path cells are the block_pitch scratch bus. Writers: JSFX fills the
// payload then GS_REB_PUB_ACK LAST; bridge presets the ACK to 0 per
// request. Keep in sync with rk_lua_core.lua GMEM.REB_*.
GS_REB_PUB_ACK     = 26320808;  // JSFX: echoes GS_REB_PUB_REQ after payload, before CMD ack
GS_REB_FAIL_BITS   = 26320809;  // JSFX: pad_fail_bits snapshot (also refreshed by CMD 88)
GS_REB_PUB_COUNT   = 26320810;  // JSFX: non-empty path cells published
GS_REB_SKIPPED     = 26320811;  // JSFX: >258-char paths dropped (unstageable in 260-cell protocol)
GS_REB_RESTORE_GEN = 26320812;  // JSFX: deserialize counter (0 = never restored)
GS_REB_PUB_REQ     = 26320813;  // producer: unique request nonce; the ACK echoes THIS,
                                //   not instance_id — multiple CMD-87 producers (rebase
                                //   audit, health tick, probes) share one ACK cell, so a
                                //   later publish stomping the ack must be DETECTABLE
                                //   (ack != my nonce → retry), never a silent hang
// One-shot BANK SELECTOR (2026-10-23, H13; capability 206). 0 = the publish as
// it always was (pad-main of the bank on screen, layers of bank A's slots: the
// health tick, rebase and relink read that). 1..NUM_BANKS = that bank's sixteen
// slots, pad-main AND layers, at the same band positions. The JSFX echoes the
// selector it honoured before the ACK and resets the request to 0, so a
// producer that never writes it keeps today's publish.
GS_REB_PUB_BANK      = 26320814;  // producer: 0 = as before, 1..4 = bank A..D
GS_REB_PUB_BANK_ECHO = 26320815;  // JSFX: the selector this publish honoured
// (+8..31 reserved header headroom)
GS_REB_PAD_CELLS   = 26320840;  // + pad*260 (len-prefixed pad-main paths, 16)
GS_REB_LAYER_CELLS = 26325000;  // + (pad*MAX_LAYERS+L)*260 (64 layer paths)
GS_REB_SLEN        = 26341640;  // + pad: s_len
GS_REB_LLEN        = 26341656;  // + pad*MAX_LAYERS+L: l_len
GS_REB_LAYERCNT    = 26341720;  // + pad: p_layer_cnt (layered/promoted-single/legacy)
// PER-SLOT control band: stride 8 keyed by _reg_my_slot (16 slots). Each
// cell has exactly ONE writer:
//   +0 PATHS_GEN    (JSFX, every @block) — bumped by loaders/clear/adopt/
//                    deserialize; bridge invalidates its publish cache on it
//   +1 HEALTH_BITS  (bridge) — audio-bearing pads w/ missing/implausible file
//   +2 HEALTH_STAMP (bridge, unix time)  +3 HEALTH_GEN (bridge: PATHS_GEN
//                    the health was computed against; @serialize trusts only
//                    an exact match)
//   +4 REBASE_UNFIXED (bridge: pads still failed after auto-rebase — banner
//                    short-circuit)  +5 REBASE_DONE stamp (bridge)  +6..7 rsvd
GS_REB_SLOT_BASE   = 26342000;  // ..26342127
// EON_DIAG: RT self-instrumentation (go-live hardening plan 0.1, 2026-09-08).
// Header +0 ARM (a probe writes 1; unless armed nothing below runs -- the
// unarmed cost is one gmem read and two branches per block, and NO writes),
// +1 RESET_GEN (bump to zero the counters; echoed at +10 of the record).
// Per-slot record at EON_DIAG_SLOT_BASE + _reg_my_slot*16: +0 SEQ (= the
// _bl_blkctr heartbeat, written LAST), +1 samplesblock, +2 srate, +3 stall_n
// (block gap > 2 periods and <= 50 ms), +4 pause_n (gap > 50 ms = the
// engine-paused class the gap detector already flushes on), +5 gap_max s,
// +6 cost_last s, +7 cost_max s, +8 cost_ema s (alpha 1/32), +9 ratio_max
// (cost / block period), +10 reset_echo, +11 overrun_n (cost > period),
// +12 blocks counted, +13 @block-pass EMA s, +14 sample-loop EMA s (split at a
// first-@sample stamp), +15 the last CMD-87 path publish's own wall time s (0 =
// none since reset; .dev_tests/EON_Live_P87Cost.lua reads it).
// Cost = t(last @sample of the block) - t(@block entry)
// = THIS FX's wall time per block. Gaps are a stall PROXY only: anticipative
// FX processing delivers @block in bursts. Cost is the loader metric.
EON_DIAG_BASE        = 26342400;  // header ..26342415
EON_DIAG_SLOT_BASE   = 26342416;  // + slot*EON_DIAG_SLOT_STRIDE ..26342671
EON_DIAG_SLOT_STRIDE = 16;
EON_DIAG_SLOT_MAX    = 16;
KIT_GMEM_BRIDGE_ALIVE = 99;   // Lua bridge heartbeat (unix timestamp)
KIT_GMEM_UNDO_ACK    = 95;    // bridge → JSFX: undo block is open (1=ready)
KIT_GMEM_UNDO_DESC   = 96;    // undo description ID (read by Lua bridge CMD 46)
KIT_GMEM_LOCK        = 97;    // instance lock (0=free, instance_id=locked)
KIT_GMEM_INSTANCE    = 98;    // instance_id of requesting JSFX
// ─── Per-instance identity bands (unified single-source-of-truth, P1) ──────
// Each instance publishes its OWN registry-slot region every @block (ungated);
// consumers pair per slot. Placed in the verified-free gap [25.16M..32.52M]
// (above stretch audio, below stretch control). Full rationale in rk_lua_core.lua.
// Per-pad VER (offset 0) is written LAST so multi-word (name) readers can retry.
INST_IDENT_BASE        = 26000000;  // slot*INST_STRIDE + pad*PAD_FIELDS + field
// Kit-categories band (BRIDGE-owned, we only READ; Spec_Swing_Kit_Categories §7a).
// Per-pad {VER,CAT,SRC,LOCK}; CAT = 46-vocab index (rk_cat_glyphs ids); VER==0 =
// never published -> pad badge falls back to the pad number.
EON_PADCAT_BASE        = 26003000;  // slot*64 + pad*4 + field
EON_PADCAT_STRIDE      = 64;
// The step sequencer's factory presets (S3b, 2026-10-20): Steppa's hand-off bands, asked and read on THIS instance's
// registry slot (rk_seq_ui asks, rk_seq_core takes; the bridge serves every slot: eon_preset_nav_tick / _stage_apply).
EON_SS_APPLY_BASE      = 26044000;  // the apply mailbox: +0 the slot it is for, +1 seq (bumped LAST), +2 rows, +3 steps, +4 steps per beat,
                                    //   +5 the ratchet list's stamp (= +1 when the list is this preset's), +6 swing %, +7 hat swing % (S3b)
EON_SS_APPLY_DATA      = 26044008;  // the 16 x 16 velocity plane, row x steps + step (0 = off)
EON_SS_APPLY_SD        = 26044264;  // the sparse ratchet list: count, then per cell: row x steps + step, hits, v1..v8
EON_SS_APPLY_HATS      = 26044990;  // S3b: a bit per plane row that is a hat row (the hat swing's lanes); an older bridge leaves 0
EON_SS_PCTRL_BASE      = 26045000;  // the preset strip, slot x 64: +0 NAV_SEQ (ours, bumped last), +1 NAV_DIR, +2 CUR_IDX, +3 COUNT,
EON_SS_PCTRL_STRIDE    = 64;        //   +5 SELECT_SEQ / +6 SELECT_IDX (the browser's), +16.. the preset's name (31 chars, 0-ended)
EON_SS_BROWSER_OPEN_REQ = 26046100; // a bump: the bridge opens the preset browser on EON_SS_BROWSER_SLOT's slot (a toggle while one is open)
EON_SS_BROWSER_SLOT    = 26046102;
// The regions (S4, 2026-10-20): the courier's bands, by Steppa's names. Swing raises SYNCON on its slot and the SWINGSEQ
// flag (+60) beside it; the courier then publishes the region MAP, the song CHAIN and the names for the slot and skips
// the pushes into a StepSeq, the zoom on select and the loop points (eon_courier_tick).
EON_SS_SYNC_BASE       = 26030000;  // slot x 64: +11 SYNCON, +60 SWINGSEQ (S4), +15 / +20 a region clicked in the Drum Matrix (pattern, bump),
EON_SS_SYNC_STRIDE     = 64;        //   +16 NEW_REQ, +17 REN_REQ, +18 OP_ORD, +19 DEL_REQ, +54 COL_REQ, +44..47 SONG OP / A1 / A2 / REQ
EON_SS_MAP_BASE        = 26160200;  // slot x 512: +0 GEN (bumped last), +1 COUNT, +2 + i*4 start QN / end QN / pattern / colour,
EON_SS_MAP_STRIDE      = 512;       //   +260 + i*3 the region's name (12 chars, four seven-bit chars a cell); the small-things round:
                                    //   the pattern is the region's FIXED LINK for a Swing slot (ExtState EON_DRUM_MATRIX:pattern_link;
                                    //   ordinal - 1 until the link, and for a Steppa slot), +452 the count of the spans this Swing's
                                    //   PRINT SONG items cover (0..29), +454 + k*2 start QN / end QN (rk_seq_core SEQ_MAP_SPAN)
EON_SS_MAP_MAXRGN      = 64;
EON_SS_SONG_BASE       = 26028000;  // slot x 112: +0 GEN, +1 LEN, +2 PLAYING, +3 CURENT (1-based, 0 = the engine idle), +4 LOOP,
EON_SS_SONG_STRIDE     = 112;       //   +5 LOOP_LIT (0 off / 1 region / 2 song) and +6 LOOP_REGION (the ordinal when +5 is 1), both
                                    //   derived by the bridge every tick (the small-things round), +8 + e*2 ordinal + repeats x 256,
                                    //   +9 + e*2 the colour
EON_SS_SONG_ENTRY_MAX  = 32;
EON_PADCAT_ADAPT       = 26004600;  // the bridge's kit-load permutation: +0 seq (last), +1 slot, +2..17 the pad each pad's sound moved to
EON_SEQ_PLIST_BASE     = 26420000;  // the preset list the bridge publishes once per run (S3b): the sequencer's own browser reads it;
// EON_SEQ_PLIST_MAX (832) is defined up at the memory claims: it must precede the claim that reads it (see there)
// Audio-lock masks for all four banks (BRIDGE-owned, we only READ; 2026-10-16, audit S10's remainder): the PADCAT
// band above is the bank ON SCREEN's sixteen, so a kit load into another bank could not see that bank's locks.
// Per slot: +0..3 = bank A..D's sixteen pads as a bit mask (bit = tile), +4 = VER (1 = the bridge publishes it; 0 =
// an older bridge, and swing_lcd_slot_locked falls back to the band for the bank on screen). MUST match rk_lua_core
// INST_PADLOCK_* / PADLOCK_OFF_VER.
EON_PADLOCK_BASE       = 26004100;  // slot*8 + bank; +4 = VER
EON_PADLOCK_STRIDE     = 8;
// Write-back mailbox (shared with Steppa's icon picker): [0]=seq LAST [1]=slot
// [2]=pad's MIDI note [3]=glyph id (-1 = Auto/re-infer). Bridge is the sole
// band writer; the CATEGORY pill posts here (rk_swing_lcd §9b).
EON_PADCAT_REQ         = 26004500;
// Lua → JSFX big-view request: +0 = seq (written LAST), +1 = target instance
// slot, +2 = VIEW_* id. Until this existed there was NO way to reach the big
// views from outside the plugin — swing_bigview_open is only ever called from
// click handlers — so nothing could drive Swing through its own screens. Added
// for the manual-capture generator; equally the hook a loader/controller would
// want. Band declared in .refs/gmem_regions_supplement.tsv.
// ── EON_FXPICK ──  moved UP to the freemem allocator (search for
// "EON_FXPICK: the FX picker's"), because swing_fxview_init sizes itself
// from FXP_REC_MAX and so the constants must precede the call. The band is
// still declared in .refs/gmem_regions_supplement.tsv.

EON_VIEW_REQ           = 26004520;
// EON_MASTER_LINK: the master section's OUTPUT STAGE, published every @block
// for EON Output on the Audio bus in Multi-Out (slot*32: +0 HB written LAST,
// +1 master_db, +2 lim_on, +3 lim_thr linear, +4 lim_rel ms). Output follows
// this record by our stable instance id, so Swing's MASTER VOL and limiter
// drive the folder even though Swing's own main bus is empty there.
EON_MASTER_LINK        = 26005248;
EON_MASTER_LINK_STRIDE = 32;

// GS_BC_LINK: the comp link band. EON Weld publishes its settings and its gain
// reduction onto a row of this band every @block; which row is decided by the
// Link Slot Lua pushes into it. ⚠️ THE ROW CARRIES THE ROLE — a Swing can own
// two Welds (smash return, and the serial glue on its Audio folder) and the row
// is keyed by slot alone, so the bus one is given registry slot + ROW_BUS and
// the smash one keeps the low rows. Full layout and the reasoning live at the
// band constants in EON_Weld.jsfx; read that before touching this.
// TWO-WAY as of 3.0.17. We READ +0 the heartbeat and +9 gain reduction in dB,
// and we WRITE the nine comp params round-robin, one per block, via the mailbox
// below -- move the COMP page or move the folder Weld and the other follows.
// (This said "we only read ... nothing here drives the folder yet" until the
// link landed; an auditor read it as the contract.)
GS_BC_LINK_BASE        = 26170000;
GS_BC_LINK_STRIDE      = 24;
GS_BC_LINK_ROW_BUS     = 32;   // audio-bus row = _reg_my_slot + this
BCL_OFF_HB             = 0;
BCL_OFF_ECHO           = 1;   // +1..+8: thresh ratio attack release knee makeup mix bypass
BCL_OFF_GR             = 9;
BCL_OFF_AUTO           = 10;  // auto-release echo — NOT part of the +1..+8 run
BCL_OFF_GRMIN          = 13;  // deepest LINEAR gain in the block (1.0 = none)
BCL_OFF_GRVER          = 14;  // 1 = that Weld publishes GRMIN; 0 = older, use +9
BCL_OFF_SEQ            = 16;  // bumped LAST, after PARAM and VAL
BCL_OFF_PARAM          = 17;  // 1..8 in echo order, 9 = auto-release
BCL_OFF_VAL            = 18;
_bcl_tx                = 0;   // round-robin cursor over the nine params
_bcl_seq               = 0;   // our command counter for the row
_bcl_primed            = 0;   // 0 = the rack has not been adopted yet this session
// What the bridge says is actually on the Audio folder. MUST match
// rk_lua_core.lua GS_STRIP_OFF_RACK_*. Lets this plugin tell "no rack at all"
// from "a rack that cannot follow me" — both mean its own compressor is wrong
// to run, but only one of them has anything to report on the COMP page.
GS_STRIP_OFF_RACK_HB   = 640;
GS_STRIP_OFF_RACK_ENG  = 641;
_rck_hb_prev           = -1;    // -1 = unbaselined; see the @block rack read
_rck_t                 = -1000; // wall clock of the last rack-scan movement (or held block while playing)
_rck_mv_t              = -1000; // wall clock of the last real rack-scan movement (the play-start re-arm)
_rck_play_prev         = 0;     // play_state & 1 on the previous block
RCK_STALE_S            = 3.0;   // no movement for this long = the rack is gone
bcl_foreign            = 0;   // 1 = a rack is there and it is not one we drive

// ── EON Tone link: the EQ + drive record ───────────────────────────────────
// In the reserved tail of this instance's strip band. Same shape as the comp
// link — heartbeat, echo run, command mailbox with the seq bumped LAST — and
// for the same reasons, so read the comp block above for the reasoning; only
// the param list differs. ONE Tone per Swing, so the registry slot alone keys
// the record and there is no role offset like GS_BC_LINK needs.
// The thirteen are Tone's own slider order, so the ids here and the ids there
// are the same integers.
TNL_OFF_HB             = 642;
TNL_OFF_ECHO           = 643;  // 643..655, params 1..13, contiguous — no gap like the comp row's GR cell
TNL_OFF_ECHO_Q         = 659;  // 659..663, params 14..18: master-EQ Q (ser_ver 75). NOT appended at
                               // 656: SEQ/PARAM/VAL live there. The first 13 keep their exact cells,
                               // so an older Tone still understands them. Use tnl_eoff(), never the
                               // arithmetic -- there are two ranges now.
TNL_OFF_SEQ            = 656;  // bumped LAST
TNL_OFF_PARAM          = 657;  // 1..13
TNL_OFF_VAL            = 658;
_tnl_hb_prev           = -1;   // -1 = unbaselined; see the @block heartbeat read
_tnl_stall             = 1000;
_tnl_row_last          = -1;   // row this baseline belongs to; -1 = none yet
_tnl_tx                = 0;
_tnl_seq               = 0;
_tnl_primed            = 0;
_tnl_noq               = 0;   // 1 = the peer never echoed a Q param (predates ser_ver 75): 14..18 are not pushed (2026-10-16)
tnl_live               = 0;    // 1 = an EON Tone is answering on our record

function tnl_get(pi) (
  pi ==  1 ? gfx_hpf_freq    : pi ==  2 ? gfx_lpf_freq    :
  pi ==  3 ? gfx_eq_lo       : pi ==  4 ? gfx_eq_lo_freq  :
  pi ==  5 ? meq_lo_bell     : pi ==  6 ? gfx_eq_mid      :
  pi ==  7 ? gfx_eq_mid_freq : pi ==  8 ? gfx_eq_hi       :
  pi ==  9 ? gfx_eq_hi_freq  : pi == 10 ? meq_hi_bell     :
  pi == 11 ? gfx_sat_drv     : pi == 12 ? gfx_drv_mode    :
  pi == 13 ? meq_bypass      : pi == 14 ? gfx_eq_lo_sq    :
  pi == 15 ? gfx_eq_lo_bq    : pi == 16 ? gfx_eq_mid_q    :
  pi == 17 ? gfx_eq_hi_sq    : gfx_eq_hi_bq;
);
// Clamped to Tone's own slider ranges on the way in — the echo is another
// plugin's memory, and these are the ranges it will quantize to anyway.
function tnl_set(pi, v) (
  pi ==  1 ? gfx_hpf_freq    = max(20, min(8000, v))     :
  pi ==  2 ? gfx_lpf_freq    = max(200, min(20000, v))   :
  pi ==  3 ? gfx_eq_lo       = max(-12, min(12, v))      :
  pi ==  4 ? gfx_eq_lo_freq  = max(40, min(500, v))      :
  pi ==  5 ? meq_lo_bell     = v >= 0.5                  :
  pi ==  6 ? gfx_eq_mid      = max(-12, min(12, v))      :
  pi ==  7 ? gfx_eq_mid_freq = max(200, min(8000, v))    :
  pi ==  8 ? gfx_eq_hi       = max(-12, min(12, v))      :
  pi ==  9 ? gfx_eq_hi_freq  = max(2000, min(16000, v))  :
  pi == 10 ? meq_hi_bell     = v >= 0.5                  :
  pi == 11 ? gfx_sat_drv     = max(0, min(1, v))         :
  pi == 12 ? gfx_drv_mode    = max(0, min(4, v | 0))     :
  pi == 13 ? meq_bypass      = v >= 0.5                  :
  pi == 14 ? gfx_eq_lo_sq    = max(0.3, min(6, v))       :
  pi == 15 ? gfx_eq_lo_bq    = max(0.3, min(6, v))       :
  pi == 16 ? gfx_eq_mid_q    = max(0.3, min(6, v))       :
  pi == 17 ? gfx_eq_hi_sq    = max(0.3, min(6, v))       :
                               gfx_eq_hi_bq = max(0.3, min(6, v));
);
// Half a step. The frequencies move in whole Hz, the gains in 0.1 dB, drive in
// 0.01, and the three toggles plus the drive type are integers.
function tnl_eps(pi) (
  pi ==  1 || pi ==  2 || pi == 4 || pi == 7 || pi == 9 ? 0.5   :
  pi == 11 ? 0.005 :
  pi ==  5 || pi == 10 || pi == 12 || pi == 13 ? 0.4 :
  // Q: 0.005. Tone's Q sliders step 0.0001, and its shelf default may round
  // 1/sqrt(2) to 0.7071 -- 6.8e-6 off Swing's exact value. The tolerance must
  // swallow that, or a DEFAULT would never settle and retry forever: the
  // filter-range bug of c7409b1 had exactly that shape.
  pi >= 14 ? 0.005 : 0.05;
);
// Param number -> its echo cell. Two ranges since ser_ver 75: 1..13 at
// TNL_OFF_ECHO, 14..18 at TNL_OFF_ECHO_Q. Every echo read goes through here.
function tnl_eoff(pi) (
  pi <= 13 ? TNL_OFF_ECHO + pi - 1 : TNL_OFF_ECHO_Q + pi - 14;
);

// ⚠️⚠️ IS THIS ECHO A VALUE AT ALL? Every adopt goes through here.
// The range test alone is not enough for the Q params. ser_ver 75 added cells
// 659..663; a Tone OLDER than that publishes a live heartbeat and the first
// thirteen echoes and never touches those five, so they read 0 — and 0 is not
// out of range, it sails through abs() and tnl_set() clamps it to the Q FLOOR
// of 0.3. Swing then carries 0.3 into its own master EQ the moment multi-out
// goes off (shelves want 1/sqrt(2), bells 0.8), and the prime marks the kit
// dirty, so the wrong value is saved. Silent, and it survives the session.
// ⭐A legitimate Q is 0.3..6 and can NEVER be 0, so a non-positive Q cell means
// "this peer does not speak Q", not "set Q to zero". Params 1..13 keep the old
// rule unchanged: zero is a legal gain, pan or bypass.
// The PUSH side applies the same rule since 2026-10-16: a Q param pushed TNL_Q_TRIES
// times with no echo marks the peer as one that does not speak Q (_tnl_noq), and
// 14..18 are not pushed again until an echo arrives after all or the peer changes
// (a heartbeat gap). Until then those five retried forever -- busy, not corrupting.
function tnl_echo_ok(pi, v) (
  abs(v) <= 100000 && (pi <= 13 || v > 0);
);

// Per-param helpers. The ids are Weld's OWN dispatch ids (1..8 in echo order,
// 9 = auto), deliberately, so these can be read straight against its source.
function bcl_get(pi) (
  pi == 1 ? cmp_thresh  : pi == 2 ? cmp_ratio  : pi == 3 ? cmp_attack :
  pi == 4 ? cmp_release : pi == 5 ? cmp_knee   : pi == 6 ? cmp_makeup :
  pi == 7 ? cmp_mix     : pi == 8 ? cmp_bypass : cmp_auto;
);
// Clamped to SWING's ranges coming in — the echo is another plugin's memory.
// Weld clamps identically on its side, so a healthy value passes untouched and
// the two never disagree about what a legal value is.
function bcl_set(pi, v) (
  pi == 1 ? cmp_thresh  = max(-40, min(0, v))    :
  pi == 2 ? cmp_ratio   = max(1, min(20, v))     :
  pi == 3 ? cmp_attack  = max(0.1, min(100, v))  :
  pi == 4 ? cmp_release = max(100, min(1200, v)) :
  pi == 5 ? cmp_knee    = max(0, min(12, v))     :
  pi == 6 ? cmp_makeup  = max(-12, min(12, v))   :
  pi == 7 ? cmp_mix     = max(0, min(1, v))      :
  pi == 8 ? cmp_bypass  = v >= 0.5               :
            cmp_auto    = v >= 0.5;
);
// ⚠ The echo run is NOT nine long: 1..8 sit at +1..+8, +9 is the GR cell, and
// auto-release echoes at +10.
function bcl_eoff(pi) ( pi == 9 ? BCL_OFF_AUTO : BCL_OFF_ECHO + pi - 1; );
// Half a step, per control: mix moves in 0.01, release in 1 ms, knee in 0.5,
// the toggles are 0/1, the rest in 0.1. Used for every comparison here, because
// Weld quantizes what it is handed and an exact compare never settles.
function bcl_eps(pi) (
  pi == 7 ? 0.005 : pi == 4 ? 0.5 : pi == 5 ? 0.26 : pi >= 8 ? 0.5 : 0.05;
);
_bcl_hb_prev           = -1;   // -1 = unbaselined; see the @block heartbeat read
_bcl_stall             = 1000; // starts stalled: nothing has proven itself live
_bcl_row_last          = -1;   // row this baseline belongs to; -1 = none yet
bcl_live               = 0;    // 1 = a bus Weld is answering on our row
bcl_gr_lin             = 1;    // linear gain, 1.0 = no reduction (needle at rest)

_view_req_last         = -1;   // seq echo; -1 = not yet baselined
_bank_pub_last         = -1;   // step 4a: the bank the publishers last saw (-1 = republish on the first block)
banktabs_drop_hl       = -1;   // step 4b: the bank tab a dragged kit card would land in (the kits view sets it while a card is dragged; -1 = none)
banktabs_menu_bank     = -1;   // step 4c: the bank whose tab menu is open (SP_POPUP_CALLER_BANK_TAB)
_undo_clear_banks      = 0;    // step 4c: 1 = the pending CLEAR (_undo_pending 1) empties all four banks, not just the visible one
// Lua → JSFX modal-surface request: +0 = seq (written LAST), +1 = target
// instance slot, +2 = kind, +3 = pad index. Companion to EON_VIEW_REQ and for
// the same reason — the overlays and popups are reachable ONLY from click
// handlers, so nothing outside the plugin could photograph them for the manual.
// Each kind drives the REAL opener rather than reproducing its contents, so a
// captured figure can never drift from the live UI:
//   0 = close everything      1 = CATEGORY glyph overlay (icons)
//   2 = KEY-RANGE overlay     3 = pad-category picker (46-vocab menu)
//   4 = tune-mode picker (Repitch / Tuned / Stretch)
// Kinds 5-8 are view SUB-STATES rather than modal cards, and +3 carries a mode
// value instead of a pad: 5 = mapping layout 0..6 (keys / 8-pad / 16-pad /
// keys+8 / keys+16 / push / notemap), 6 = KIT-tab panel 0..3 (none / NOTES /
// OUT / LAYERS), 7 = push sub-mode, 8 = 8-pad bank.
// 9 and 10 are modal cards again: 9 = embed menu (knobs / icons / TCP / MCP),
// 10 = controller note-map presets (the 16-preset list). 11 raises the
// "Kit samples missing" banner for a figure (+3 = pad count shown) via a
// display-only flag, and 12 opens that banner's Relink / Load / Dismiss menu.
// Band declared in .refs/gmem_regions_supplement.tsv.
EON_POPUP_REQ          = 26004540;
_popup_req_last        = -1;   // seq echo; -1 = not yet baselined
_relink_demo_n         = 0;    // display-only "Kit samples missing" trigger for
                               // the manual generator (kind 11). 0 = off. See
                               // rk_swing_ui_state's banner gate for WHY this is
                               // separate from pad_fail_bits.
// Change-map band (BRIDGE-owned, we only READ; Spec_Swing_Change_Map_And_Reroll
// §3.2): what the LAST kit operation did to each pad, so the KIT-tab grid can
// report it. SEQ (offset 0) written LAST, same retry discipline as PADCAT.
// Sits above EON_PADCAT_ADAPT (26004600 + 0..17); 26004700..26005211 verified
// free 2026-07-29 against every gmem map incl EON/.Extension/src/gmem/*.h.
// Pad codes: 0 empty, 1 changed, 2 changed-shared(cycle), 3 locked, 4 custom,
// 5 no-match, 6 synth. 0 and 5 are DIFFERENT (nothing here vs looked+found
// nothing); 6 keeps synth pads out of 5.
EON_CHGMAP_BASE        = 26004700;  // slot*32 + offset
EON_CHGMAP_STRIDE      = 32;
// ─── Root-note band (BRIDGE-owned publisher; we only READ) ────────────────
// Per-pad detected root note for the PITCH readout. Same publish discipline as
// PADCAT/IDENT: VER (offset 0) is written LAST, so a reader that sees VER>0 is
// guaranteed the other fields of that record are complete.
//
// ⚠️ PER-INSTANCE ON PURPOSE. The legacy GS_PAD_KEY_BASE (1416-1431) is a FLAT
// 16-cell band with no slot stride — two Swing instances overwrite each other's
// readout. That band stays write-only/legacy; this one replaces it for display.
//
// SMP pads: the bridge runs rk_root_note.lua (clean-room YIN) and publishes
// here. SYN pads do NOT need the band at all — rk_synthdrums knows its settled
// fundamental in closed form, so the synth path can compute the note locally
// and exactly (SRC_SYNTH); noise families (hat/cym) have no fundamental and
// correctly show nothing.
// Band claimed in .refs/gmem_regions_supplement.tsv (26006000..26008063).
EON_ROOTNOTE_BASE      = 26006000;  // slot*128 + pad*8 + field
EON_ROOTNOTE_STRIDE    = 128;       // 16 pads * 8 fields
EON_ROOTNOTE_FIELDS    = 8;
RN_OFF_VER   = 0;   // monotonic; 0 = never published. WRITTEN LAST.
RN_OFF_NOTE  = 1;   // MIDI note 0..127; -1 = no root note (unpitched/gated)
RN_OFF_CENTS = 2;   // -50..+50
RN_OFF_CONF  = 3;   // 0..1 (YIN aperiodicity complement)
RN_OFF_SRC   = 4;   // 0 = none, 1 = detected (YIN), 2 = synth (exact)
RN_SRC_NONE = 0; RN_SRC_DETECTED = 1; RN_SRC_SYNTH = 2;
// Re-analysis request mailbox (JSFX -> bridge). Seq written LAST.
EON_ROOTNOTE_REQ       = 26008048;  // +0 seq, +1 slot, +2 pad (-1 = all), +3 rsvd
CHGMAP_OFF_SEQ       = 0;   // monotonic, written LAST
CHGMAP_OFF_OP        = 1;   // 0 none, 1 LOAD, 2 FILL, 3 REROLL_KIT, 4 REROLL_PAD
CHGMAP_OFF_N_CHG     = 2;
CHGMAP_OFF_N_LOCK    = 3;
CHGMAP_OFF_N_CUSTOM  = 4;
CHGMAP_OFF_N_NOMATCH = 5;
CHGMAP_OFF_SURPLUS   = 6;
CHGMAP_OFF_STAMP     = 7;   // time_precise() at publish; reader expires on age
CHGMAP_OFF_PADS      = 8;   // + pad (0..15) -> outcome code
CHGMAP_EXPIRE_S      = 900;
// Kits-view roster band (BRIDGE-owned publisher; we READ + bump REQ only.
// Spec_Swing_Kits_View.md §3; claimed in gmem_regions_supplement.tsv).
EON_KITLIST_BASE     = 26240000;  // +0 SEQ (even=stable) +1 GEN +2 kits +3 folders +4 ver +5 REQ +6 heartbeat +7 DEV pick mailbox (probes; MAGIC+idx+1, see below)
// Devpick trigger sentinel: probes write KV_DEVPICK_MAGIC + record index + 1
// into +7. The magic window keeps a stray count/index/instance_id (or an
// os.time()-scale heartbeat overshoot) from ever firing a synthetic kit load —
// the consume site range-checks [MAGIC, MAGIC+100000).
KV_DEVPICK_MAGIC     = 424200000;
EON_KITLIST_FOLDERS  = 26240032;  // 31 x 32: [0]=len, [1..31]=chars
EON_KITLIST_RECORDS  = 26241024;  // 128 x 56: [0]=len [1..40]=name [41]=folder [42]=type [43]=pads [44]=KB // 15 min: an optimistic value must never live forever
// Kit cover artwork path exchange (claimed in gmem_regions_supplement.tsv).
// BOTH directions live in this one PER-INSTANCE band on purpose: it costs no CMD
// number, and it keeps cover paths off GS_BROWSER_PATH — that is a CMD-serialised
// SHARED bus with an in-flight latch (rk_swing_browser_load.jsfx-inc:43), so a
// cover staged there would race sample loads.
// Paths use the length-prefixed form ([0]=len, [1..len]=chars, [1+len]=0, <=258),
// the same convention as GS_MIGR/GS_REB_PAD_CELLS.
EON_KITCOVER_BASE      = 26251792;  // + _reg_my_slot * STRIDE
EON_KITCOVER_STRIDE    = 544;
KITCOVER_OFF_PUB_SEQ   = 0;    // bridge -> JSFX, written LAST after the path
KITCOVER_OFF_PUB_PATH  = 1;    // extracted temp-file path of the loaded kit's cover
KITCOVER_OFF_PUB_PREVIEW = 261; // 1 = unsaved drop preview (keep the UNSAVED cue up)
KITCOVER_OFF_PEND_SEQ  = 272;  // JSFX -> bridge, written LAST after the path
KITCOVER_OFF_PEND_PATH = 273;  // path of a just-dropped image, awaiting the next save
KITCOVER_PATH_MAX      = 258;
INST_IDENT_INST_STRIDE = 128;       // 16 pads * 8 fields
INST_IDENT_PAD_FIELDS  = 8;
IDENT_OFF_VER = 0; IDENT_OFF_HUE = 1; IDENT_OFF_MUTE = 2; IDENT_OFF_SOLO = 3;
IDENT_OFF_NOTE = 4; IDENT_OFF_OUTPUT = 5; IDENT_OFF_ICON = 6;
IDENT_OFF_AUDIO = 7;  // explicit blank state: 1 = loaded, -1 = blank, 0 = old
                      // build (consumers fall back to the hue<=-1.5 sentinel).
                      // Needed because hue -2 is ALSO the manual-BLACK color —
                      // hue alone made consumers wipe a black pad's identity.
INST_PADNAME_BASE        = 26010000;  // slot*INST_STRIDE + pad*32 chars (0-term)
INST_PADNAME_INST_STRIDE = 512;       // 16 pads * 32
INST_PADNAME_PAD_LEN     = 32;
// ─── All-bank identity + name bands (2026-10-22, Plan_Swing_All_Bank_Note_Names: the MIDI editor names every bank's pads) ──
// The sixteen-pad bands above carry the bank ON SCREEN (seven readers assume it). These carry all sixty-four pads
// (bank x 16 + pad) with the same eight fields and 32-char names: the notes, blank flags and names compared every
// block (the names against a shadow string per pad, ID64NAME_STR_BASE), the other fields on the heal blocks,
// rewritten only where it differs; the bank on screen plays no part. The bridge's note-name walker rebuilds a
// track's names whole from them when +1 GEN moves. In the
// free gap above EON_SEQ_PRINT (ends 31535551), under STRETCH_CONTROL (32524288); declared in the supplement.
INST_IDENT64_BASE        = 31540000;  // slot x 528: +0 STAMP (1 = this instance publishes these bands), +1 GEN (a pad's NOTE, AUDIO or
INST_IDENT64_INST_STRIDE = 528;       //   name changed; written LAST), +2 PUBS (passes), +3 FGEN (any field), +4..15 spare;
INST_IDENT64_HDR         = 16;        //   +16 + (bank * 16 + pad) * 8 + field (INST_IDENT's eight fields)
IDENT64_OFF_STAMP = 0; IDENT64_OFF_GEN = 1; IDENT64_OFF_PUBS = 2; IDENT64_OFF_FGEN = 3;
INST_PADNAME64_BASE        = 31550000;  // slot x 2048: (bank * 16 + pad) * 32 chars (0-ended)
INST_PADNAME64_INST_STRIDE = 2048;
// Per-instance pad MIX publish (gain/pan). The IDENT band is FULL at 8 fields,
// so these get their own small band rather than a stride change that would
// relocate every identity consumer. Purely a READ surface for remote control
// surfaces (Steppa's lane VOL/PAN knobs) that need to rest a control on the
// pad's real value; the INCMD_GAIN/PAN mailboxes stay the only write path back,
// so this band has exactly one writer (us) and never needs a seqlock — single
// floats are word-atomic, published every block like the rest of the pass.
// Placed in the verified-free gap between PADNAME's end (26010000 + 16*512 =
// 26018192) and StepSeq's M/S band (26020000); 16 slots * 32 -> ..26019511.
INST_PADMIX_BASE         = 26019000;  // + slot*INST_PADMIX_INST_STRIDE + pad*2
INST_PADMIX_INST_STRIDE  = 48;        // 16 pads * 2 fields, then 16 spare (32..47)
PADMIX_OFF_GAIN = 0;                  // linear gain, matches INCMD_GAIN payload
PADMIX_OFF_PAN  = 1;                  // -1..1, matches INCMD_PAN payload
// Knob APPEARANCE tail (32..35) — the four hidden sliders that decide how this
// instance draws its pad VOL/PAN knobs. Published so a remote surface can render
// the SAME knob rather than a lookalike: Steppa's lane knobs run the identical
// style+appear resolution chain (rk_swing_ui_grid_pads.jsfx-inc:926-949) against
// its own lane hue. Values are the raw slider ints, not resolved colours —
// appear==7 means "follow pad colour", which only the drawing side can resolve
// because it owns the hue it is drawing against.
PADMIX_OFF_VOL_STYLE  = 32;           // 0 = follow theme (sk_kp), 1..18 = style id
PADMIX_OFF_VOL_APPEAR = 33;           // 0 = accent, 1..6 preset, 7 = pad colour, 8 blk, 9 wht
PADMIX_OFF_PAN_STYLE  = 34;
PADMIX_OFF_PAN_APPEAR = 35;           // 0 = accent2 (NOT accent — the pair differ by default)
// Inbound per-instance command mailboxes (IN direction, Increment D). External
// writers (bridge TCP mirror, browser, Pad-FX) post pad color/name commands
// HERE — never into the owner-published bands above. Payload first, flag LAST;
// this instance consumes in @block by zeroing the flag. Flag 1 = adopt
// silently (writer owns the undo point), 2 = adopt + mark_dirty_pad.
INST_INCMD_BASE   = 26100000;  // slot*INST_INCMD_STRIDE + region offsets
INST_INCMD_STRIDE = 1024;      // 16 slots -> 26100000..26116383 (free gap)
INCMD_COLOR_OFF   = 0;         // + pad*2: [0]=flag, [1]=hue payload 0..1
INCMD_NAME_OFF    = 64;        // + pad*34: [0]=flag(LAST), [1]=gen, [2..33]=chars
INCMD_NAME_FIELDS = 34;
// Mute/solo SET commands (Increment E): absolute 0/1 payloads. Four regions of
// 32 (16 pads * [flag,val]) starting at INCMD_MUTE_OFF, in this order:
// +0 bridge mute, +32 bridge solo, +64 sequencer mute, +96 sequencer solo —
// separate writer-origin regions keep every cell single-writer.
INCMD_MUTE_OFF     = 640;
INCMD_SOLO_OFF     = 672;
INCMD_SEQ_MUTE_OFF = 704;
INCMD_SEQ_SOLO_OFF = 736;
// P4 — note/output/reverse cells (browser-origin; every writer is a user
// action so flag is always 2 = adopt + mark_dirty_pad). REVERSE is the one
// TOGGLE-semantics cell (payload ignored): reverse has no published band
// field to diff a SET against, and a lost toggle is visible + re-clickable.
INCMD_NOTE_OFF = 768;   // + pad*2: [0]=flag, [1]=MIDI note 0..127
INCMD_OUT_OFF  = 800;   // + pad*2: [0]=flag, [1]=output pair 0..15
INCMD_REV_OFF  = 832;   // + pad*2: [0]=flag, [1]=unused (toggle)
// SFZ-import fidelity: SET per-pad params the CMD-63 audio load doesn't carry.
INCMD_TUNE_OFF = 864;   // + pad*2: [0]=flag, [1]=semitones -24..24
INCMD_GAIN_OFF = 896;   // + pad*2: [0]=flag, [1]=linear gain 0..8
INCMD_PAN_OFF  = 928;   // + pad*2: [0]=flag, [1]=pan -1..1
INCMD_LMODE_OFF= 960;   // + pad*2: [0]=flag, [1]=layer mode 0..3 (RS5k import)
// The per-pad flag of NOTE / TUNE / GAIN / PAN / LMODE: 1 or 2 = the tile in the bank on screen when the cell is
// taken (every writer until 2026-10-23); 2 + 4 x (bank + 1) = the tile in THAT bank, whatever bank shows then
// (the browser's SFZ / RS5k import, audit H26 round 2: the whole mailbox is held while kit_busy, so a post can
// wait many blocks, and a tab switch in between sent one bank's tune / gain / pan / note / layer mode to another).
function swing_incmd_slot(tile, flag) local(b) (
  b = (flag / 4) | 0;
  b >= 1 && b <= NUM_BANKS ? (b - 1) * NUM_PADS + tile : swing_bp(tile);
);
// Lane color ownership view cells (per-slot, NOT per-pad; source of truth is
// P_EXT on the track, bridge-owned — nothing serialized here):
//   PUB (bridge->us, republished each identity pass): 0=unpublished,
//       1=swing 2=reaper 3=none. REQ (us->bridge): [+0]=flag LAST, [+1]=mode.
INCMD_LANEPOL_PUB = 992;
INCMD_LANEPOL_REQ = 994;
KIT_GMEM_INSTANCE_NEXT = 94;  // monotonic counter for new instance_id allocation
                              // (replaces time_precise() which had a 10µs collision window)
KIT_COPY_CHUNK       = 200000; // samples per frame during audio copy
// Kit-export dump (state 11, rk_swing_ui_state): copies walk in KIT_DUMP_CHUNK
// pieces (half of EEL2's 2^20 loop cap — a plain pad's slot is 4M cells), and
// the dump must end below KIT_GMEM_AUDIO_DUMP_END, where the Stretch rings
// begin (.refs/swing_gmem_bridge_protocol.md §3: KIT_GMEM_AUDIO's safe
// ceiling is 16,777,215). Spec_Swing_Long_Pad_Layer_Cap §4.3-4.4.
KIT_DUMP_CHUNK          = 524288;
KIT_GMEM_AUDIO_DUMP_END = 16777216;
// ─── VER-26 per-pad kit-load handshake (mirrors rk_lua_core GMEM.HS_*) ─────
// Spec: .docs/specs/Spec_Swing_PerPad_Sidecar_Load.md. Band 26500000-26509999
// claimed 2026-07-07 (inside the documented free gap, below stretch control).
KIT_HS_GEN   = 26500000; // bridge publish generation (odd=writing, even=ready)
KIT_HS_ECHO  = 26500001; // our echo: last generation fully copied
KIT_HS_PAD   = 26500002; // target pad 0..15
KIT_HS_LAYER = 26500003; // layer index (0 = pad-main blob)
KIT_HS_LEN   = 26500004; // samples staged in the AUDIO window
KIT_HS_FLAGS = 26500005; // bit0=first-blob-of-pad (memset slot), bit1=kit-done
KIT_HS_CAP   = 26500006; // we advertise 26 every @block (bridge capability check)

