  // dock_want (ser_ver 69) survives that, so the first frame of a fresh window
  // session that finds itself wanting the dock and not in it re-posts exactly
  // what the click would have -- the bridge's eon_redock_tick then selects our
  // track and launches or reuses the pane. Same shape as the mini browser's
  // hello (5481a65): persisting a state that used to be reachable only by a
  // gesture silently dropped what that gesture also did.
  //
  // "Fresh window session" = a gap in @gfx frames. @gfx only runs while the
  // window is showing, so a >1 s gap is the window having been closed; the
  // first frame ever qualifies too (_dock_gfx_t starts at 0). ONE ask per
  // session on purpose: a pane that cannot launch (Hub present, script
  // missing) already tells the user so once, and a retry loop would make that
  // a message-box storm. It waits for a live bridge rather than spending the
  // ask on a dead one.
